  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result (80 digits)\n\n**Formal expansion over the 24 SoV labels does not exist.**\n- The abstract determinant has 242 monomials, all with the per-site split $Q_1^2Q_2$ on each site.\n- Only 96 of them are monomials of the physical $\\Psi_A(x)$. These carry about 3% of the coefficient weight.\n- The least-squares fit $\\det N=\\sum_x c_x\\Psi_A(x)$ therefore has relative residual $\\approx 1$, for both $w$.\n- The remaining monomials (Q's at non-SoV points) can only be reduced through state A's Baxter equation.\n\n**On-shell definition.** $c_x$ is fixed by $\\det N(A,\\Omega_w)/\\Psi_A(x_0)=\\sum_x c_x\\langle x|\\Psi_A\\rangle$ for all 24 twist-$z$ states A. This is unique because the $\\langle x|R_A\\rangle$ matrix is invertible, and it would agree with any formal expansion if one existed.\n\n| check | $w=(5/2,7/3,6/35)$ | control $w=z$ |\n|---|---|---|\n| $\\langle V\\|$ factorises (σ₂/σ₁ as 8×3) | 4×10⁻⁶⁸ | 4×10⁻⁷⁸ |\n| line-stabiliser dim of $\\langle V\\|$ (e₂₄: 6, random: 1) | **6** | **6** |\n| $\\langle V\\|\\propto\\langle\\Omega^L_w\\|$ | yes | yes |\n| $\\langle V\\|\\propto$ left vacuum at $z$ | no | yes (and $D_A\\propto\\delta_{A,\\Omega}$) |\n| $\\langle V\\|\\propto e_{24}$ | no | no |\n\n**Conclusion.** $\\sum_x c_x\\langle x|$ is a global $GL(3)$ rotation of $\\langle 0|=e_{24}$ up to normalisation: it is exactly the left companion vacuum at twist $w$. At $w=z$ it reduces to the physical left vacuum.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary: global rotations of ⟨0| = determinants of Q-integrals at a different twist\n\n**Main point.** A global $GL(3)$ rotation of the SoV reference covector $\\langle 0|=e_{24}$ corresponds to the SoV determinant with **dual Q's taken at a different twist**.\n\n$$\\frac{\\det_{6\\times6}\\big\\langle Q^j_{\\Omega_w}\\,\\cdot\\,Q_{A,i}\\big\\rangle}{\\Psi_A(x_0)}=\\sum_x c_x(\\theta,w)\\,\\frac{\\Psi_A(x)}{\\Psi_A(x_0)}=\\langle V_w|\\Psi_A\\rangle,\\qquad \\langle V_w|=\\sum_x c_x\\langle x| \\;\\propto\\; \\langle 0|\\,\\rho(g_w).$$\n\nIn words:\n- The determinant pairs any twist-$z$ state A with the dual Q-functions of the vacuum at twist $w$.\n- Stripping off the wave functions leaves a covector $\\langle V_w|$ in the SoV basis.\n- That covector is a global rotation of $\\langle 0|$. It is the left companion vacuum at twist $w$, $\\langle\\Omega^L_w|$.\n\n**Chain of results in this notebook** (L = 2, sites [2,1,0] ⊗ [1,0,0], $\\theta=(1/3,-8/57)$, $h=1$, $z=(2,3,1/6)$):\n1. **Companion transfer matrices** from quantum minors. Their spectrum equals the diagonal-twist spectrum, and it is simple.\n2. **SoV B operator from the untwisted T.** $\\mathbf B=\\prod(u-x^\\alpha_{kj})$ with $x=\\theta+h(\\mu_{kj}-j+1)$, a non-degenerate spectrum, and $\\langle 0|=e_{24}$.\n3. **Normalised covectors.** $\\langle x|\\Psi\\rangle=\\Psi(x)/\\Psi(x_0)$ holds for all 24 eigenstates, with $\\hat q_i=z_i^{u/h}q_i$; the exponential is required.\n4. **Scalar product.** The 6×6 determinant is orthogonal and equals $\\langle L_A|R_B\\rangle/(\\langle L_A|e_{24}\\rangle\\langle e_{24}|R_B\\rangle)$ up to $C_{\\rm vac}$ (2×10⁻⁷⁸). It uses the ladder measure $\\theta_1+\\{0,1,2\\}$, $\\theta_2+\\{0,1\\}$ and the general-rep $\\Psi^{\\rm ref}$, $c^{\\rm ref}$. The implied ket reference is also $e_{24}$.\n5. **Dual vacuum at twist $w\\neq z$.** $\\langle V_w|$ factorises as adjoint ⊗ fundamental and has line-stabiliser dimension 6, so it is a rotation of $e_{24}$. It is $\\propto\\langle\\Omega^L_w|$, and at $w=z$ it reduces to the physical left vacuum.\n\n**Caveat.** With A's Q's fully abstract, $\\det N$ is **not** formally a combination of the 24 $\\Psi_A(x)$: 146 of its 242 monomials, about 97% of the weight, sit at non-SoV points. The $c_x$ are therefore fixed on-shell over the 24 eigenstates, which is unique.\n\n**Next (section 8).** A **single-site** rotation, from the one-site functional $\\langle e^{ku}q_1(u+h)\\rangle/q_1(\\theta_1+h)$ with $\\langle f\\rangle=\\oint f/((u-\\theta_1)(u-\\theta_1-h))$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 8. One-site functional → rotation of ⟨0| on site 1 only\n\n$$\\langle f\\rangle=\\sum_{p\\in\\{\\theta_1,\\theta_1+h\\}}\\frac{f(p)}{\\prod_{p'\\neq p}(p-p')}=\\frac{f(\\theta_1+h)-f(\\theta_1)}{h},\\qquad f(u)=e^{ku}q_{A,1}(u+h).$$\n\n- Here $q_{A,1}$ is the polynomial part of state A's $Q_1$, and $e^{ku}$ is read as the exponential in the integration variable.\n- **Formal expansion with abstract $q$.** $q_1(\\theta_1+2h)/q_1(\\theta_1+h)=z_1^{-h}\\,\\Psi_A(x')/\\Psi_A(x_0)$, where $x'$ is $x_0$ with only the site-1 root $x_{11}$ raised ($\\lambda_{21}:1\\to2$). Hence\n$$\\frac{\\langle e^{ku}q_1(u+h)\\rangle}{q_1(\\theta_1+h)}=\\langle V_k|\\Psi_A\\rangle,\\qquad \\langle V_k|=-\\frac{e^{k\\theta_1}}{h}\\langle 0|+\\frac{e^{k(\\theta_1+h)}z_1^{-h}}{h}\\langle x'|.$$\n- **Checks.** (i) On-shell over all 24 states. (ii) $\\langle V_k|=s_k\\otimes e_3$, so site 2 is untouched. (iii) The line stabiliser of $s_k$ in the adjoint has dimension 6, a rotation of $e_8$. (iv) An explicit one-parameter group element $s_k\\propto e_8\\exp(a(k)E_{ij})$ is found, and $a(k)e^{-kh}$ is tested for $k$-independence.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 10. <e^{ku} q1(u+h)>/q1(θ1+h), measure 1/((u-θ1)(u-θ1-h)): <V_k| = c0 <0| + c1 <x'|, rotation on site 1 only? ---- *)\nClearAll[xPrime, qq, kk, bracket1, formal1, coefV, Vk, site1Data, site1Tab, stabAdj, e8, JJad, poles1];\nxPrime = {{{0}, {2, 0}, λ1}, x0[[2]]};\n(* formal bracket with an abstract function qq *)\nbracket1 = Module[{ps1 = {θ1, θ1 + h}}, Sum[Exp[kk p] qq[p + h]/Times @@ (p - DeleteCases[ps1, p]), {p, ps1}]/qq[θ1 + h]];\nformal1 = Expand[bracket1];\n(* coefficients of <0| and <x'| : q1(θ1+2h)/q1(θ1+h) = z1^-h Ψ(x')/Ψ(x0) *)\ncoefV[k_] := {-Exp[k θ1]/h, Exp[k (θ1 + h)] zX[[1]]^(-h)/h} /. prmX;\nVk[k_] := coefV[k] . {xNorm[x0], xNorm[xPrime]};\n\ne8 = UnitVector[d1, d1];\nJJad[i_, j_] := JJ[i, j, λ1];\n(* line stabiliser in the adjoint: {X : s.ρ(X) ∈ C s} *)\nstabAdj[s_] := 10 - numRank[Transpose[Append[Flatten[Table[s . JJad[i, j], {i, 3}, {j, 3}], 1], -s]], 10^-50];\npoles1 = {θ1, θ1 + h} /. prmX;\n\nsite1Data[k_] := Module[{V = N[Vk[k], wpS], D, onShell, mat, sv, s, site2, stab, dirs},\n   (* the bracket evaluated on each actual state A (polynomial q1, twist z) *)\n   D = Table[With[{q1 = stS[[A, \"q\", 1]]},\n      Sum[Exp[N[k p, wpS]] (q1 /. u -> p + hX)/Times @@ (p - DeleteCases[poles1, p]), {p, poles1}]/(q1 /. u -> poles1[[2]])], {A, dtot}];\n   onShell = Max[Abs[V . Rhat - D]]/Max[Abs[D]];\n   mat = Partition[V, d2]; sv = SingularValueList[mat, Tolerance -> 0];\n   site2 = Max[Abs[mat[[All, {1, 2}]]]]/Max[Abs[mat]];\n   s = mat[[All, d2]]; s = s/s[[d1]];\n   stab = stabAdj[s];\n   (* explicit one-parameter subgroup: s = e8 + a e8.E with e8.E.E = 0 *)\n   dirs = Select[Flatten[Table[{i, j}, {i, 3}, {j, 3}], 1],\n     #[[1]] != #[[2]] && (e8 . JJad @@ #) =!= ConstantArray[0, d1] && (e8 . JJad[#[[1]], #[[2]]] . JJad[#[[1]], #[[2]]]) === ConstantArray[0, d1] &&\n       numRank[{s - e8, e8 . JJad @@ #}, 10^-50] == 1 &];\n   <|\"k\" -> k, \"onShell\" -> onShell, \"svRatio\" -> sv[[2]]/sv[[1]], \"site2\" -> site2, \"stab\" -> stab, \"dirs\" -> dirs,\n     \"a\" -> If[dirs === {}, Missing[], With[{v = e8 . JJad @@ dirs[[1]]}, With[{p = First @ Ordering[-Abs[v], 1]}, (s - e8)[[p]]/v[[p]]]]],\n     \"stabGlobal\" -> stabDim[V]|>];\n\nsite1Tab = site1Data /@ {0, 1/2, -3/5, 2};\nColumn[{\n  Grid[{\n    {\"formal bracket (abstract qq)\", formal1},\n    {\"x' valid SoV label / site-1 roots (x11,x21,x22)\", {MemberQ[patPairs, xPrime], xRoots[1, xPrime[[1]]]}},\n    {\"control: adjoint stabiliser of e_8 / random\", {stabAdj[N[e8, wpS]], stabAdj[N[Table[Prime[i]/(i + 2), {i, d1}], wpS]]}}\n   }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[Table[{d[\"k\"], sci[d[\"onShell\"]], sci[d[\"svRatio\"]], sci[d[\"site2\"]], d[\"stab\"], d[\"stabGlobal\"], d[\"dirs\"],\n       If[MissingQ[d[\"a\"]], \"-\", N[d[\"a\"], 12]], If[MissingQ[d[\"a\"]], \"-\", N[d[\"a\"] Exp[-d[\"k\"] hX], 12]]}, {d, site1Tab}],\n    {\"k\", \"on-shell <V_k|R_A> = bracket (24 states)\", \"σ₂/σ₁ (8×3)\", \"site-2 part off e_3\", \"adjoint stabiliser dim of s_k (6 ⇔ rotation)\",\n     \"global stabiliser dim of <V_k|\", \"direction E_ij, s = e8 exp(a E_ij)\", \"a(k)\", \"a(k) e^{-kh}\"}],\n   Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
