       "data": "Out[128]= \\begin{matrix}\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{formal bracket (abstract qq)} & \\frac{\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{kk}\\,\\left(h+\\theta1\\right)}\\,\\mathrm{qq}\\left(2\\,h+\\theta1\\right)}{h\\,\\mathrm{qq}\\left(h+\\theta1\\right)}-\\frac{\\mathrm{e}^{\\theta1\\,\\mathrm{kk}}}{h}\\\\\\hline\\text{x' valid SoV label / site-1 roots (x11,x21,x22)} & \\left\\{\\mathrm{True},\\left\\{2\\,h+\\theta1,\\theta1,\\theta1-h\\right\\}\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{control: adjoint stabiliser of e\\_8 / random} & \\left\\{6,3\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}\\\\\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{k} & \\text{on-shell <V\\_k|R\\_A> = bracket (24 states)} & \\text{$\\sigma$₂/$\\sigma$₁ (8$\\times$3)} & \\text{site-2 part off e\\_3} & \\text{adjoint stabiliser dim of s\\_k (6 $\\Leftrightarrow$ rotation)} & \\text{global stabiliser dim of <V\\_k|} & \\text{direction E\\_ij, s = e8 exp(a E\\_ij)} & \\text{a(k)} & \\text{a(k) e\\^{}\\{-kh\\}}\\\\\\hline0 & \\text{0.}\\times 10^{\\text{-74}} & \\text{0} & \\text{0} & 6 & 5 & \\begin{pmatrix}3 & 2\\end{pmatrix} & -0.5 & -0.5\\\\\\hline\\frac{1}{2} & \\text{0.}\\times 10^{\\text{-74}} & \\text{0} & \\text{0} & 6 & 5 & \\begin{pmatrix}3 & 2\\end{pmatrix} & -0.824360635350 & -0.5\\\\\\hline-\\frac{3}{5} & \\text{0.}\\times 10^{\\text{-74}} & \\text{0} & \\… [latex truncated: 1440 chars total]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "5908cb2b-0cdb-4818-9a3c-0762765ea683"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result (80 digits; k = 0, 1/2, −3/5, 2)\n\n- **Exact two-term expansion.** With abstract $q$, the bracket is $\\frac{\\langle e^{ku}q_1(u+h)\\rangle}{q_1(\\theta_1+h)}=-\\frac{e^{k\\theta_1}}{h}+\\frac{e^{k(\\theta_1+h)}}{h}\\frac{q_1(\\theta_1+2h)}{q_1(\\theta_1+h)}=\\langle V_k|\\Psi_A\\rangle$ with $\\langle V_k|=-\\frac{e^{k\\theta_1}}{h}\\langle 0|+\\frac{e^{k(\\theta_1+h)}z_1^{-h}}{h}\\langle x'|$. The on-shell residual over all 24 states is 0 to working precision.\n- **Site 2 untouched.** $\\langle V_k|=s_k\\otimes e_3$ exactly: rank 1 as an 8×3 matrix, and the site-2 factor is exactly $e_3$.\n- **Rotation on site 1.**\n  - The adjoint line stabiliser of $s_k$ has dimension **6**; the controls give 6 for $e_8$ and 3 for a generic covector.\n  - The global stabiliser of $\\langle V_k|$ has dimension 5, so this is *not* a global rotation.\n  - Explicitly, with $\\rho$ = `JJ[i,j,{2,1,0}]` acting on covectors from the right:\n$$s_k\\propto e_8\\,\\exp\\!\\big(a(k)\\,\\rho(E_{32})\\big),\\qquad a(k)=-\\tfrac12\\,e^{kh}\\quad(\\text{all four }k),$$\n    where $e_8\\rho(E_{32})^2=0$.\n  - The $-\\tfrac12$ is consistent with $a(k)=-z_1^{-h}e^{kh}$ ($z_1=2$), but only one twist was tested.\n- **Summary.** The one-site bracket $\\langle e^{ku}q_1(u+h)\\rangle/q_1(\\theta_1+h)$ is $\\langle 0|\\big(e^{a(k)E_{32}}\\otimes 1\\big)|\\Psi_A\\rangle$ up to normalisation: a rotation of $\\langle 0|$ on the first site only, along the nilpotent direction $E_{32}$, with parameter $\\propto e^{kh}$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 9. Survey: which minors of the scalar-product matrix are SoV expansions, and which are global rotations?\n\n**Matrix.** Rows $(\\alpha,i,j)$ with $\\alpha\\in\\{1,2\\}$, $i,j\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$; columns $u^\\beta(-Q^jQ_{A,i},\\ Q^jQ^{[-2]}_{A,i},\\ Q^{j[2]}Q_{A,i})$, $\\beta=0,1$. The measure is the same as in section 6. State B is fixed to the dual Q's of the vacuum at twist $w=(5/2,7/3,6/35)$.\n\n**Candidate minors.** $\\Psi_A(x)$ has degree 6 in state A's Q's with content $Q_1^4Q_2^2$. So only the 6×6 minors with four $i=1$ rows and two $i=2$ rows can match: $\\binom{6}{4}\\binom{6}{2}=225$. The scalar product of section 6 is one of them.\n\n**Criterion for \"expands into wave functions\".**\n- A formal expansion in abstract Q's already fails for the scalar product (section 7).\n- An on-shell expansion over the 24 states always exists, so on its own it tests nothing.\n- The meaningful requirement is that the coefficients depend only on $(\\theta,w)$ and **not on the chain's twist**. So $c_x$ is solved from $\\det/\\Psi_A(x_0)=\\sum_x c_x\\Psi_A(x)/\\Psi_A(x_0)$ on all 24 eigenstates at twist $z=(2,3,1/6)$, and again at an independent unimodular twist $z'=(3/2,5/4,8/15)$. The two solutions must coincide.\n- Only the Q-functions enter $\\Psi_A(x)/\\Psi_A(x_0)$, so this needs no covector normalisation.\n\n**Rotation test** for minors that pass. Build $\\langle V|=\\sum_x c_x\\langle x|_z$ and require line-stabiliser dimension 6. Also record whether $\\langle V|\\propto\\langle\\Omega^L_w|$.\n\n**Consistency check of the criterion.** The normalised covectors $\\langle x|_z$ and $\\langle x|_{z'}$ are compared as well. If they coincide, then $z$-independence of $c_x$ is the same statement as $z$-independence of $\\langle V|$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 11. Minor survey: 225 minors (four i=1 rows, two i=2 rows) vs twist-w vacuum; z-independence of c_x (up to scale); rotation test. ---- *)\nClearAll[zP, wM, chainM, psiG, rowN, rowKeys12, minorSets, minorData, survey, knownSet, classOf, cMonomial, monoControl];\nzP = {3/2, 5/4, 8/15}; wM = {5/2, 7/3, 6/35};\n\n(* Ψ(x) with twist zz; exponent (x-θ)/h, the dropped constant cancels in ratios *)\npsiG[qs_, zz_][p_] := Product[With[{xr = xRoots[s, p[[s]]] /. prmX, θa = {θ1, θ2}[[s]] /. prmX},\n    With[{qh = Function[{i, x}, zz[[i]]^((x - θa)/hX) (qs[[i]] /. u -> x)]},\n     qh[1, xr[[1]]] Det[{{qh[1, xr[[2]]], qh[1, xr[[3]]]}, {qh[2, xr[[2]]], qh[2, xr[[3]]]}}]]], {s, 2}];\n\n(* full companion chain at twist zz: eigenstates (80 digits), q1,q2, P[A,x] = Ψ_A(x)/Ψ_A(x0), normalised covectors *)\nchainM[zz_] := chainM[zz] = Module[{pz = prmOf[zz], coT, gen, vecs, eig, sts, P, vac1, om, qOm, xn},\n   coT = Table[Coefficient[τ[a], u, k] /. pz, {a, 2}, {k, 0, 4}];\n   eig[v_, a_] := With[{i = First @ Ordering[Abs[N[v]], -1]}, Sum[(coT[[a, k + 1]] . v)[[i]]/v[[i]] u^k, {k, 0, 2 a}]];\n   gen = Sum[Prime[3 + 2 a + k] coT[[a, k + 1]], {a, 2}, {k, 0, 2 a - 1}];\n   vecs = Eigenvectors[N[gen, wpS]];\n   sts = Table[<|\"vec\" -> v, \"q\" -> Table[baxSolve[eig[v, 1], eig[v, 2], zz[[i]]], {i, 2}]|>, {v, vecs}];\n   P = Table[psiG[s[\"q\"], zz][p]/psiG[s[\"q\"], zz][x0], {s, sts}, {p, patPairs}];\n   vac1 = Expand[Sum[zz[[i]] ν[i][u], {i, 3}] /. pz];\n   om = First @ NullSpace[Join @@ Table[coT[[1, k + 1]] - Coefficient[vac1, u, k] IdentityMatrix[dtot], {k, 0, 2}]];\n   om = om/om[[dtot]];\n   qOm = Table[baxSolve[eig[om, 1], eig[om, 2], zz[[i]]], {i, 2}];\n   xn = Table[With[{vx = First[xCov[p]]}, vx (psiG[qOm, zz][p]/psiG[qOm, zz][x0])/(vx . om)], {p, patPairs}];\n   <|\"z\" -> zz, \"states\" -> sts, \"P\" -> P, \"xNorm\" -> xn, \"failed\" -> !FreeQ[sts[[All, \"q\"]], $Failed]|>];\n\n(* numeric row (α,i,j) for direct q's qs at twist zz against dual q's qd at twist w *)\nrowN[qs_, zz_, qd_, w_, {α_, i_, j_}] := Sum[With[{p = polesSP[[r]]},\n    With[{QD = Function[x, Exp[N[x, wpS] Log[N[zz[[i]], wpS]]] (qs[[i]] /. u -> x)], QU = Function[x, Exp[-N[x, wpS] Log[N[w[[j]], wpS]]] (qd[[j]] /. u -> x)]},\n     wSP[[r]] Exp[2 Pi I (α - 1) N[p, wpS]/hX] Flatten @ Table[p^β {-QU[p] QD[p], QU[p] QD[p - hX], QU[p + hX] QD[p]}, {β, 0, 1}]]],\n   {r, Length[polesSP]}];\n\nrowKeys12 = Flatten[Table[{α, i, j}, {α, 2}, {i, 2}, {j, 3}], 2];\nminorSets = Flatten[Table[Join[s1, s2], {s1, Subsets[Select[rowKeys12, #[[2]] == 1&], {4}]}, {s2, Subsets[Select[rowKeys12, #[[2]] == 2&], {2}]}], 1];\nknownSet = Flatten[Table[{α, ij[[1]], ij[[2]]}, {α, 2}, {ij, tripleSP}], 1];\n\nminorData = Module[{qd = vacAtTwist[wM][\"qd\"], rows, ch, res},\n   res = Table[ch = chainM[zz];\n     rows = Table[AssociationMap[rowN[s[\"q\"], zz, qd, wM, #]&, rowKeys12], {s, ch[\"states\"]}];\n     Table[Module[{D = Table[Det[Lookup[rows[[A]], ms]]/psiG[ch[\"states\"][[A, \"q\"]], zz][x0], {A, dtot}]},\n        <|\"D\" -> D, \"c\" -> LinearSolve[ch[\"P\"], D]|>], {ms, minorSets}], {zz, {zX, zP}}];\n   Table[<|\"rows\" -> minorSets[[m]], \"cz\" -> res[[1, m, \"c\"]], \"czp\" -> res[[2, m, \"c\"]]|>, {m, Length[minorSets]}]];\n\n(* pass = c_x(z) and c_x(z') agree up to an overall (twist-dependent) scale *)\nclassOf[d_] := Module[{cz = d[\"cz\"], czp = d[\"czp\"], scale, V, st, rOm, ratio},\n   scale = Max[Abs[Join[cz, czp]]];\n   If[scale < 10^-50, Return[<|\"class\" -> \"zero\"|>]];\n   If[numRank[{cz, czp}, 10^-40] == 2, Return[<|\"class\" -> \"z-dependent\"|>]];\n   ratio = With[{p = First @ Ordering[-Abs[cz], 1]}, czp[[p]]/cz[[p]]];\n   V = cz . chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"]; V = V/V[[First @ Ordering[-Abs[V], 1]]];\n   st = stabDim[V]; rOm = numRank[{V, vacAtTwist[wM][\"OmegaL\"]}, 10^-40];\n   <|\"class\" -> \"z-independent up to scale\", \"ratio\" -> ratio, \"exactEqual\" -> (Max[Abs[cz - czp]]/scale < 10^-40), \"stab\" -> st, \"propOmegaL\" -> (rOm == 1), \"V\" -> V|>];\nsurvey = Table[Join[<|\"rows\" -> d[\"rows\"]|>, classOf[d]], {d, minorData}];\n\n(* control: single per-site Q1^2 Q2 monomials must fail (c(z), c(z') independent) *)\ncMonomial[m_, zz_] := Module[{ch = chainM[zz]},\n   LinearSolve[ch[\"P\"], Table[With[{QD = Function[{i, x}, Exp[N[x, wpS] Log[N[zz[[i]], wpS]]] (s[\"q\"][[i]] /. u -> x)]},\n       Product[QD[1, m[[t, 1]]] QD[1, m[[t, 2]]] QD[2, m[[t, 3]]], {t, 2}]/psiG[s[\"q\"], zz][x0]], {s, ch[\"states\"]}]]];\nmonoControl = With[{p1 = (θ1 /. prmX) + {-1, 0, 1, 2}, p2 = (θ2 /. prmX) + {-1, 0, 1}},\n   Table[numRank[{cMonomial[m, zX], cMonomial[m, zP]}, 10^-40],\n    {m, {{{p1[[4]], p1[[4]], p1[[1]]}, {p2[[3]], p2[[1]], p2[[2]]}}, {{p1[[1]], p1[[2]], p1[[3]]}, {p2[[2]], p2[[2]], p2[[3]]}}, {{p1[[3]], p1[[4]], p1[[4]]}, {p2[[1]], p2[[3]], p2[[1]]}}}}]];\n\nModule[{zi = Select[survey, #[\"class\"] == \"z-independent up to scale\"&], known = SelectFirst[survey, Sort[#[\"rows\"]] == Sort[knownSet]&]},\n Grid[{\n   {\"chains at z, z': any Baxter solve failed?\", {chainM[zX][\"failed\"], chainM[zP][\"failed\"]}},\n   {\"normalised covectors: max |<x|_z - <x|_{z'}|\", sci[Max[Abs[Flatten[chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"] - chainM[zP][\"xNorm\"]]]]]},\n   {\"control: rank{c(z), c(z')} for 3 single monomials (2 = fails)\", monoControl},\n   {\"class counts (225 minors)\", Normal[Counts[survey[[All, \"class\"]]]]},\n   {\"known scalar-product minor: stab / ∝ Ω^L_w / c(z')/c(z)\", {known[\"stab\"], known[\"propOmegaL\"], N[known[\"ratio\"], 12]}},\n   {\"passing minors: c(z) = c(z') exactly (tally)\", Tally[zi[[All, \"exactEqual\"]]]},\n   {\"passing minors: stabiliser dims (tally)\", Tally[zi[[All, \"stab\"]]]},\n   {\"passing minors: ∝ Ω^L_w (tally)\", Tally[zi[[All, \"propOmegaL\"]]]},\n   {\"passing minors: span dim of all <V|\", If[zi === {}, 0, numRank[zi[[All, \"V\"]], 10^-40]]},\n   {\"passing minors: distinct scale ratios c(z')/c(z)\", Length[Union[Round[Re[zi[[All, \"ratio\"]]] 10^30]]]}\n  }, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"24223\" data-output-id=\"11\" data-out-n=\"142\" data-sub-idx=\"19\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"25\" data-sub-start=\"60\" data-sub-end=\"72\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[142]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:12.08em;vertical-align:-5.77em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.31em;\"><span style=\"top:-8.27em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.27em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:12.04em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-5.77em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.27em;\"><span style=\"top:-8.43em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">chains at z, z’: any Baxter solve failed?</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">normalised covectors: max |&lt;x|_z - &lt;x|_{z’}|</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.03em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">control: rank{c(z), c(z’)} for 3 single monomials (2 = fails)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.83em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">class counts (225 minors)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.62em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">known scalar-product minor: stab / </span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∝</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"> Ω</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">L_w / c(z’)/c(z)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">passing minors: c(z) = c(z’) exactly (tally)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.2em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">passing minors: stabiliser dims (tally)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:0.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">passing minors: </span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∝</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"> Ω</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">ˆ</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">L_w (tally)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:1.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">passing minors: span dim of all &lt;V|</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">passing minors: distinct scale ratios c(z’)/c(z)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.77em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:12.04em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-5.77em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.27em;\"><span style=\"top:-8.43em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">False</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">False</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.03em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.83em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">z-independent up to scale</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">225</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.62em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">{</span></span><span class=\"mord\">6</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.755794856798</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mb