  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Answer: the reachable rotations form a 2-parameter surface\n\nAll statements below are **exact** (rational arithmetic), except the $e^{ku}$ dressing and the non-vacuum rows (80 digits).\n\n**Closed form.** For the scalar-product determinant against the dual Q's of the vacuum at unimodular twist $w$,\n$$\\langle V|=\\langle\\Omega^L_w|\\;\\propto\\;\\langle 0|e^{aE_{21}}e^{bE_{31}}e^{cE_{32}},\\qquad\n\\boxed{a=-w_1w_2,\\quad b=w_1,\\quad c=-w_1(w_2+w_3)}$$\nverified with zero residual on 6 twists. $(a,b,c)$ does **not** depend on $\\theta$ (checked at three inhomogeneity points).\n\n**The constraint.** Eliminating $w$ (with $w_1w_2w_3=1$) leaves one relation,\n$$\\boxed{b=a(c-a)}\\qquad\\Longleftrightarrow\\qquad c=a+\\frac ba,$$\nso the construction covers a **codimension-1 surface** in the 3-dimensional space of global rotations, not all of it.\n\n**Inverse map.** Every $(a,b,c)$ on that surface comes from exactly one twist,\n$$w=\\Big(b,\\;-\\frac ab,\\;-\\frac1a\\Big),\\qquad w_1w_2w_3=1\\ \\text{automatically},$$\nchecked exactly on four targets (residual 0).\n\n**The $e^{ku}$ dressing adds nothing.** Inserting $e^{ku}$ in every row gives $(a,b,c)\\to(ae^k,be^{2k},ce^k)$, which preserves $b=a(c-a)$ exactly. The Jacobian of $(w_1,w_2,k)\\mapsto(a,b,c)$ is degenerate: its determinant falls with the finite-difference step ($6\\times10^{-16}$ at step $10^{-15}$, $-5\\times10^{-41}$ at step $10^{-40}$), so the rank is 2.\n\n**Examples.** Pure $E_{32}$ rotations $(0,0,c)$ satisfy $b=a(c-a)$ and are reachable. Pure $E_{21}$ rotations $(a,0,0)$ with $a\\neq0$ are **not**.\n\n**Non-vacuum dual Q's do not help.** Replacing the vacuum at $w_0$ by another eigenstate gives covectors that are not rotations at all (stabiliser dims 5, 5, 3, 3 for states 1, 2, 5, 20; only the vacuum, index 9 here, gives 6 with zero residual).\n\n**Open.** Reaching $b\\neq a(c-a)$ needs a genuinely different construction: e.g. dual Q's from different twists per index $j$, extra columns/powers, or products with one-site brackets of the section-8 type (those move a single site and are not constrained to this surface).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 11. The six vacua $\\tau_1=\\sum_i w_{\\sigma(i)}\\nu_i$\n\nEach permutation $\\sigma$ gives a state whose left eigenvector is again a global rotation, but a Weyl-translated one: only $\\sigma=\\mathrm{id}$ lies in the big cell $\\langle 0|e^{aE_{21}}e^{bE_{31}}e^{cE_{32}}$. So each covector is fitted in every Bruhat cell $\\langle 0|W\\,e^{aE_{21}}e^{bE_{31}}e^{cE_{32}}$, with $W$ running over the six Weyl elements built from $s_i=e^{E_{i,i+1}}e^{-E_{i+1,i}}e^{E_{i,i+1}}$.\n\nFor each $\\sigma$: solve the dual Baxter equation for that state, build the same $6\\times6$ determinant, extract $c_x$ on-shell at $z$ and $z'$, and then test (i) twist-independence, (ii) stabiliser dimension 6, (iii) which cell $W$ and which $(a,b,c)$, (iv) whether the surface relation $b=a(c-a)$ still holds in that cell.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 14. The six vacua t1 = Sum_i w_{sigma(i)} nu_i: dual Q's, determinant, and which rotation they give. ---- *)\nClearAll[permStates, weylEls, uW, VsymW, fitCell, permTab, permData];\npermStates[w_] := permStates[w] = Module[{pz = prmOf[w], coT},\n   coT = Table[Coefficient[τ[a], u, k] /. pz, {a, 2}, {k, 0, 4}];\n   Table[Module[{t1 = Expand[Sum[w[[σ[[i]]]] ν[i][u], {i, 3}] /. pz], ns, om, i0, t2},\n      ns = NullSpace[Join @@ Table[coT[[1, k + 1]] - Coefficient[t1, u, k] IdentityMatrix[dtot], {k, 0, 2}]];\n      If[Length[ns] =!= 1, <|\"σ\" -> σ, \"dim\" -> Length[ns]|>,\n       om = First[ns]; i0 = First @ Ordering[-Abs[om], 1];\n       t2 = Sum[((coT[[2, k + 1]] . om)[[i0]]/om[[i0]]) u^k, {k, 0, 4}];\n       <|\"σ\" -> σ, \"dim\" -> 1, \"t1\" -> t1, \"t2\" -> t2, \"qd\" -> Table[baxSolveDual[t1, t2, 1/w[[j]]], {j, 3}]|>]],\n    {σ, Permutations[Range[3]]}]];\n\n(* Weyl elements as products of s_i = e^{E_{i,i+1}} e^{-E_{i+1,i}} e^{E_{i,i+1}} in the 24-dim rep *)\nweylEls = With[{s = Table[nilExpT[Normal@Etot[i, i + 1], 1] . nilExpT[Normal@Etot[i + 1, i], -1] . nilExpT[Normal@Etot[i, i + 1], 1], {i, 2}]},\n   {IdentityMatrix[dtot], s[[1]], s[[2]], s[[1]] . s[[2]], s[[2]] . s[[1]], s[[1]] . s[[2]] . s[[1]]}];\nuW = Table[UnitVector[dtot, dtot] . W, {W, weylEls}];\nVsymW = Table[Expand[uu . nilExpT[Normal@Etot[2, 1], aa] . nilExpT[Normal@Etot[3, 1], bb] . nilExpT[Normal@Etot[3, 2], cc]], {uu, uW}];\n(* fit V in each cell: read parameters off components that are a NUMBER times a single parameter, then check the whole covector *)\nfitCell[V_] := Module[{best = <|\"res\" -> Infinity|>},\n   Do[Module[{Vs = VsymW[[n]], i0, tn, ids, pars, res, pure},\n     pure[e_, v_] := With[{co = Coefficient[e, v]}, co =!= 0 && FreeQ[co, aa | bb | cc] && e === co v];\n     i0 = SelectFirst[Range[dtot], (Vs[[#]] =!= 0 && FreeQ[Vs[[#]], aa | bb | cc])&, Missing[]];\n     If[MissingQ[i0], Continue[]];\n     tn = (V/V[[i0]]) Vs[[i0]];\n     ids = Table[SelectFirst[Range[dtot], pure[Vs[[#]], v]&, Missing[]], {v, {aa, bb, cc}}];\n     If[MemberQ[ids, _Missing], Continue[]];\n     pars = Table[tn[[ids[[m]]]]/Coefficient[Vs[[ids[[m]]]], {aa, bb, cc}[[m]]], {m, 3}];\n     res = Max[Abs[(Vs /. Thread[{aa, bb, cc} -> pars]) - tn]]/Max[Abs[tn]];\n     If[res < best[\"res\"], best = <|\"cell\" -> n, \"abc\" -> pars, \"res\" -> res|>]], {n, Length[VsymW]}];\n   best];\n\npermData = Table[Module[{st = permStates[w0][[m]], cs, V, f},\n    If[st[\"dim\"] =!= 1, <|\"σ\" -> st[\"σ\"], \"bad\" -> True|>,\n     cs = Table[With[{ch = chainM[zz]}, LinearSolve[ch[\"P\"], Table[Det[rowNk[s[\"q\"], zz, st[\"qd\"], w0, 0, #]& /@ knownSet]/psiG[s[\"q\"], zz][x0], {s, ch[\"states\"]}]]], {zz, {zX, zP}}];\n     If[Max[Abs[cs[[1]]]] < 10^-50, <|\"σ\" -> st[\"σ\"], \"zero\" -> True|>,\n      V = cs[[1]] . chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"]; f = fitCell[V];\n      <|\"σ\" -> st[\"σ\"], \"degs\" -> (Exponent[#, u]& /@ st[\"qd\"]), \"rankZ\" -> numRank[cs, 10^-40], \"stab\" -> stabDim[V/Max[Abs[V]]],\n        \"cell\" -> Lookup[f, \"cell\", \"no cell\"], \"abc\" -> Lookup[f, \"abc\", {}], \"res\" -> f[\"res\"],\n        \"surf\" -> If[KeyExistsQ[f, \"abc\"], f[\"abc\"][[2]] - f[\"abc\"][[1]] (f[\"abc\"][[3]] - f[\"abc\"][[1]]), Missing[]]|>]]], {m, 6}];\n\npermTab = Table[If[KeyExistsQ[d, \"abc\"] && d[\"abc\"] =!= {},\n    {d[\"σ\"], d[\"degs\"], d[\"rankZ\"], d[\"stab\"], d[\"cell\"], N[d[\"abc\"], 8], sci[Abs[d[\"res\"]]], sci[Abs[d[\"surf\"]]]},\n    {d[\"σ\"], \"-\", \"-\", \"-\", \"-\", If[TrueQ[d[\"zero\"]], \"det vanishes\", \"no cell / eigenspace not 1-dim\"], \"-\", \"-\"}], {d, permData}];\nGrid[Prepend[permTab, {\"σ (t1 = Σ_i w_{σ(i)} ν_i)\", \"dual Q degrees\", \"rank{c(z),c(z')}\", \"stabiliser dim\", \"Bruhat cell W\", \"(a,b,c) in that cell\", \"fit residual\", \"|b - a(c-a)|\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
