   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result: the six vacua stay on the same surface\n\nAll six states $\\tau_1=\\sum_i w_{\\sigma(i)}\\nu_i$ at $w_0=(5/2,7/3,6/35)$ exist with a 1-dimensional eigenspace, their dual Baxter equations solve (degrees are the permuted $(3,1,0)$), and the same $6\\times6$ determinant is non-zero for each.\n\nFor every $\\sigma$ (80 digits):\n- twist-independent up to scale (rank 1 at $z$ vs $z'$),\n- **line-stabiliser dimension 6**, so each is a global rotation,\n- all six land in the **big cell** ($W=1$), with fit residual 0,\n- the closed form is simply the permuted one,\n$$(a,b,c)_\\sigma=\\big(-w_{\\sigma(1)}w_{\\sigma(2)},\\; w_{\\sigma(1)},\\; -w_{\\sigma(1)}(w_{\\sigma(2)}+w_{\\sigma(3)})\\big),$$\n  matching to working precision for all six,\n- and therefore $b-a(c-a)=0$ for all six.\n\n**So the six vacua give six different points, but no new rotations**: since $\\sigma(w)$ is again an unimodular triple, each $\\sigma$ sweeps the *same* surface $b=a(c-a)$ as $w$ varies. The determinant against any vacuum-type dual Q's at a single twist stays on that codimension-1 surface. Combined with the earlier scans (all 225 minors, the $e^{ku}$ dressing, non-vacuum dual states), the surface is not left by any of these deformations.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 12. The two-site analogue of the one-site bracket\n\n$$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}\\langle e^{ku}q_1(u+h)\\rangle_1 & \\langle e^{ku}u\\,q_1(u+h)\\rangle_1\\\\[2pt] \\langle e^{ku}q_1(u+h)\\rangle_2 & \\langle e^{ku}u\\,q_1(u+h)\\rangle_2\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\langle f\\rangle_s=\\!\\!\\sum_{p\\in\\{\\theta_s,\\theta_s+h\\}}\\!\\!\\mathop{\\rm Res}_{u=p}\\frac{f(u)}{\\nu_3(u)\\nu_3(u-h)} .$$\n\n$\\nu_3(u)\\nu_3(u-h)=\\prod_s(u-\\theta_s)(u-\\theta_s-h)$ has four simple poles, so each residue weight keeps the other ladder's factors; $\\langle\\cdot\\rangle_s$ encircles only its own ladder.\n\nThe object is degree 2 in $q_1$ (one value per row), so it can only move $x_{11}$ on each site, with the rest of the label at $x_0$. Two shift conventions are tested:\n- **as written**: $q_1(u+h)$ on both sites, sampling $\\theta_s+h,\\theta_s+2h$;\n- **per-site**: $q_1(u+h\\lambda^{(s)}_2)$, i.e. $q_1(u+h)$ at the adjoint site and $q_1(u)$ at the fundamental site, which matches each site's own $x_{11}$ range ($\\{\\theta_1+h,\\theta_1+2h\\}$ and $\\{\\theta_2,\\theta_2+h\\}$) and the $\\Psi^{\\rm ref}$ rule.\n\nNormalisation is by the two $x_0$ values of $q_1$. Tests: twist-independence at $z$ vs $z'$, stabiliser dimension, whether the covector factorises, the per-site rotation parameters (global $\\Leftrightarrow$ they agree), the Bruhat cell fit, and $b-a(c-a)$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 15. Two-site bracket determinant: det_{s,col} <e^{ku} u^{col-1} q1(u+shift_s)>_s. ---- *)\nClearAll[polesTwo, wTwo, brTwo, twoDet, twoData, twoTab, fitRepSym, fitRep, siteShift];\npolesTwo = Table[{θ1, θ2}[[s]] /. prmX, {s, 2}] + # & /@ {0, hX} // Transpose;   (* {{θ1,θ1+h},{θ2,θ2+h}} *)\nwTwo = Table[1/Times @@ (polesTwo[[s, r]] - DeleteCases[Flatten[polesTwo], polesTwo[[s, r]]]), {s, 2}, {r, 2}];\n(* bracket over the ladder of site s of f, with the 4-pole measure 1/(ν3(u) ν3(u-h)) *)\nbrTwo[f_, s_] := Sum[wTwo[[s, r]] f[polesTwo[[s, r]]], {r, 2}];\nsiteShift = {{hX, hX}, {hX, 0}};   (* row 1: as written; row 2: per-site h λ2 *)\ntwoDet[qs_, zz_, k_, sh_] := Module[{QD = Function[x, Exp[N[x, wpS] Log[N[zz[[1]], wpS]]] (qs[[1]] /. u -> x)]},\n   Det[Table[brTwo[Function[p, Exp[N[k p, wpS]] p^(col - 1) QD[p + sh[[s]]]], s], {s, 2}, {col, 2}]]\n    /(QD[(θ1 /. prmX) + hX] QD[(θ2 /. prmX)])];\n(* per-rep fit of a site covector: e_low . e^{a E21} e^{b E31} e^{c E32} *)\nfitRepSym[rep_] := fitRepSym[rep] = With[{d = dim[rep]},\n   Expand[UnitVector[d, d] . nilExpT2[JJ[2, 1, rep], aa, d] . nilExpT2[JJ[3, 1, rep], bb, d] . nilExpT2[JJ[3, 2, rep], cc, d]]];\nnilExpT2[M_, t_, d_] := Module[{acc = IdentityMatrix[d], term = IdentityMatrix[d], k = 0},\n   While[k < 30, k++; term = Expand[t term . M/k]; If[Union[Flatten[term]] === {0}, Break[]]; acc += term]; acc];\nfitRep[s_, rep_] := Module[{Vs = fitRepSym[rep], d = dim[rep], i0, tn, ids, pars, pure},\n   pure[e_, v_] := With[{co = Coefficient[e, v]}, co =!= 0 && FreeQ[co, aa | bb | cc] && e === co v];\n   i0 = SelectFirst[Range[d], (Vs[[#]] =!= 0 && FreeQ[Vs[[#]], aa | bb | cc])&];\n   tn = (s/s[[i0]]) Vs[[i0]];\n   ids = Table[SelectFirst[Range[d], pure[Vs[[#]], v]&, Missing[]], {v, {aa, bb, cc}}];\n   pars = Table[If[MissingQ[ids[[m]]], 0, tn[[ids[[m]]]]/Coefficient[Vs[[ids[[m]]]], {aa, bb, cc}[[m]]]], {m, 3}];\n   {pars, Max[Abs[(Vs /. Thread[{aa, bb, cc} -> pars]) - tn]]/Max[Abs[tn]]}];\n\ntwoData[k_, sh_] := Module[{cs, V, Vn, mat, sv, s1, s2, f1, f2, fc},\n   cs = Table[With[{ch = chainM[zz]}, LinearSolve[ch[\"P\"], Table[twoDet[st[\"q\"], zz, k, sh], {st, ch[\"states\"]}]]], {zz, {zX, zP}}];\n   V = cs[[1]] . chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"]; Vn = V/V[[First @ Ordering[-Abs[V], 1]]];\n   mat = Partition[Vn, d2]; sv = SingularValueList[mat, Tolerance -> 0];\n   s1 = mat[[All, d2]]; s2 = mat[[d1]];\n   f1 = fitRep[s1, λ1]; f2 = fitRep[s2, λ2]; fc = fitCell[Vn];\n   <|\"k\" -> k, \"sh\" -> sh, \"rankZ\" -> numRank[cs, 10^-40], \"stab\" -> stabDim[Vn], \"svRatio\" -> sv[[2]]/sv[[1]],\n     \"site1\" -> f1, \"site2\" -> f2, \"cell\" -> Lookup[fc, \"cell\", \"-\"], \"abc\" -> Lookup[fc, \"abc\", {}], \"res\" -> fc[\"res\"],\n     \"surf\" -> If[KeyExistsQ[fc, \"abc\"], fc[\"abc\"][[2]] - fc[\"abc\"][[1]] (fc[\"abc\"][[3]] - fc[\"abc\"][[1]]), Missing[]]|>];\n\ntwoTab = Table[twoData[k, sh], {sh, siteShift}, {k, {0, 1/2, -1}}];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{If[d[\"sh\"] === {hX, hX}, \"as written\", \"per-site hλ2\"], d[\"k\"], d[\"rankZ\"], d[\"stab\"], sci[d[\"svRatio\"]],\n     N[d[\"site1\"][[1]], 8], sci[d[\"site1\"][[2]]], N[d[\"site2\"][[1]], 8], sci[d[\"site2\"][[2]]],\n     d[\"cell\"], N[d[\"abc\"], 8], sci[Abs[d[\"res\"]]], If[MissingQ[d[\"surf\"]], \"-\", sci[Abs[d[\"surf\"]]]]}, {d, Flatten[twoTab, 1]}],\n   {\"shift\", \"k\", \"rank{c(z),c(z')}\", \"stab dim\", \"σ₂/σ₁ (8×3)\", \"site-1 (a,b,c)\", \"site-1 res\", \"site-2 (a,b,c)\", \"site-2 res\", \"cell\", \"global (a,b,c)\", \"global res\", \"|b-a(c-a)|\"}],\n  Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"24223\" data-output-id=\"26\" data-out-n=\"359\" data-sub-idx=\"14\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"35\" data-sub-start=\"34\" data-sub-end=\"38\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[359]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:8.4751em;vertical-align:-3.9676em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.5076em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.4676em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.4676em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:8.4351em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.9676em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:4.4676em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.6276em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">shift</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.4276em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">as written</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.2224em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">as written</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.0224em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"