  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result: the two-site bracket determinant gives exactly the $E_{32}$ rotations\n\n**1. As written it does not expand into wave functions.** With $q_1(u+h)$ at both sites, $c_x(z)$ and $c_x(z')$ are independent (rank 2), the stabiliser is 1 and the covector does not factorise. The cause is the fundamental site: $q_1(u+h)$ samples $\\theta_2+h,\\theta_2+2h$, while its $x_{11}$ range is $\\{\\theta_2,\\theta_2+h\\}$.\n\n**2. With the per-site shift $h\\lambda^{(s)}_2$ it does expand, but it is not a rotation — and not even a per-site one.** Exactly four labels carry weight, the $x_{11}$ offsets $\\{0,1\\}\\times\\{0,1\\}$, and $c_x$ is twist-independent. The exact coefficient matrix (normalised, $k=0$) and the two rotation families are\n\n$$\\underbrace{\\begin{pmatrix}1&-\\tfrac{28}{9}\\\\[2pt]\\tfrac{10}{9}&1\\end{pmatrix}}_{\\text{columns }\\{1,u\\}},\\qquad\n\\underbrace{\\begin{pmatrix}1&\\tfrac{47}{28}c\\\\[2pt]\\tfrac{9}{28}c&c^2\\end{pmatrix}}_{\\text{global }e^{cE_{32}}},\\qquad\n\\underbrace{\\begin{pmatrix}1&\\tfrac{47}{28}c_2\\\\[2pt]c_1-\\tfrac{19}{28}c_2&c_1c_2\\end{pmatrix}}_{e^{c_1E_{32}}\\otimes\\,e^{c_2E_{32}}}.$$\n\n- Against the **global** family: the off-diagonal ratio must be $47/9=5.22$, but the object gives $-28/10=-14/5$. Structurally $c_{12}/c_{21}=\\frac{W_1W'_2(p'_2-p_1)}{W_2W'_1(p'_1-p_2)}$ and the $e^{kp}$ factors cancel, so this ratio is **$k$-independent** and equals $-14/5$ for any $k$ — which is why `Solve` finds no $k$. Since every combination of global $E_{32}$ rotations keeps the ratio $47:9$, the object is not in their span either.\n- Against the **per-site** family: matching the first two entries gives $c_1=-0.14657$, $c_2=-1.85343=-784/423$, which then predicts $c_{22}=c_1c_2=0.27163$, but the object has $1$ (off by $-0.728$). So it is not a product of one-site rotations; consistently, its stabiliser is 5 and it fails to factorise ($\\sigma_2/\\sigma_1=0.12$).\n\n**3. The fix is the second column.** With columns $\\{1,g(u)\\}$ the coefficients are $W_iW'_j\\,(g(p'_j)-g(p_i))$, and in $c_{11}c_{22}/(c_{12}c_{21})$ the weights cancel, leaving a pure cross-ratio condition on the four values $A=g(\\theta_1),B=g(\\theta_1+h),C=g(\\theta_2),D=g(\\theta_2+h)$:\n$$\\frac{(C-A)(D-B)}{(D-A)(C-B)}=\\frac{784}{423}.$$\n$g(u)=u$ fails it; the solved $g$ satisfies it to 12 digits. The parameter is then $c=\\frac{28}{47}\\frac{W'_2(D-A)}{W'_1(C-A)}$.\n\n**4. Tuned, it is a global rotation.** For $k=0,\\ 1/2,\\ -1$: twist-independent (rank 1), **stabiliser 6**, $(a,b,c)=(0,0,c_0)$ with residual $\\sim10^{-93}$, and $c_0\\propto e^{kh}$ (complex; $g$ itself is complex, two conjugate branches). Choosing $k=0.7232\\,i$ gives $c_0=1$ exactly.\n\n**Conclusion.** A $2\\times2$ determinant of one-site brackets is a global rotation exactly when its column values satisfy the cross-ratio condition, and it then produces the **pure $E_{32}$ rotations** $(0,0,c)$ — degree 2 in $q$, no $6\\times6$ needed. These already satisfy $b=a(c-a)$, so they lie inside the surface of section 10. Leaving that surface needs an object that moves $x_{21}$, not just $x_{11}$.\"",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 13. Free two-term weights: a global $E_{32}$ rotation from a $2\\times2$ determinant\n\nNow the brackets are general two-term functionals **evaluated at each site's own $x_{11}$ points**,\n$$\\langle f\\rangle_1=a_1f(\\theta_1+h)+b_1f(\\theta_1+2h),\\qquad \\langle f\\rangle_2=a_2f(\\theta_2)+b_2f(\\theta_2+h),$$\n$$\\mathcal D=\\det\\begin{pmatrix}\\langle e^{ku}q_1\\rangle_1&\\langle e^{ku}u\\,q_1\\rangle_1\\\\ \\langle e^{ku}q_1\\rangle_2&\\langle e^{ku}u\\,q_1\\rangle_2\\end{pmatrix}\\Big/\\big(q_1(\\theta_1+h)q_1(\\theta_2)\\big).$$\nExpanding, $\\mathcal D=\\sum_{i,j}W_iW'_j\\,(p'_j-p_i)$ with $W_1=a_1e^{kp_1},W_2=b_1e^{kp_2},W'_1=a_2e^{kp'_1},W'_2=b_2e^{kp'_2}$, on the points $p=(\\theta_1+h,\\theta_1+2h)$, $p'=(\\theta_2,\\theta_2+h)$.\n\n**Why this version can work.** In $c_{11}c_{22}/(c_{12}c_{21})$ the weights cancel, leaving the cross-ratio of the four points. With $t=\\theta_2-\\theta_1$ it is $\\frac{t(t-2h)}{(t-h)^2}$, and the rotation pattern needs exactly $\\frac{784}{423}$ — **identical** here ($t=-9/19$, both $=784/423$). Indeed the pattern constants are themselves pole ratios: $\\tfrac{47}{28}=\\frac{t-2h}{t-h}$, $\\tfrac{9}{28}=\\frac{t}{t-h}$. (In section 12 the insertion $u$ sat at the pole while $q_1$ was shifted, which spoiled this.)\n\n**Solving the two remaining equations** for the weight ratios gives, for a target $c$,\n$$\\boxed{\\ \\frac{b_1}{a_1}=c\\,e^{-kh}\\,\\frac{t}{t-2h},\\qquad \\frac{b_2}{a_2}=c\\,e^{-kh}\\,\\frac{t-2h}{t}\\ }$$\nand then $c_{22}/c_{11}=c^2$ follows automatically. Only the combination $ce^{-kh}$ enters, so $k$ is redundant and can be set to 0; no complex parameters are needed.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 17. Free-weight two-site determinant: solve b_s/a_s for a target global rotation e^{c E32}. ---- *)\nClearAll[tPar, ptsSite, rOf, detFree, freeRun, freeTab];\ntPar = (θ2 - θ1) /. prmX;\nptsSite = {{(θ1 /. prmX) + hX, (θ1 /. prmX) + 2 hX},    (* site-1 x11 points: θ1+h, θ1+2h *)\n           {(θ2 /. prmX), (θ2 /. prmX) + hX}};          (* site-2 x11 points: θ2, θ2+h   *)\n(* weight ratios b_s/a_s that produce the global rotation e^{c E32} *)\nrOf[cval_, k_] := {cval Exp[-k hX] tPar/(tPar - 2 hX), cval Exp[-k hX] (tPar - 2 hX)/tPar};\ndetFree[qs_, zz_, k_, rr_] := Module[{QD = Function[x, Exp[N[x, wpS] Log[N[zz[[1]], wpS]]] (qs[[1]] /. u -> x)]},\n   Det[Table[Sum[{1, rr[[s]]}[[m]] Exp[N[k ptsSite[[s, m]], wpS]] ptsSite[[s, m]]^(col - 1) QD[ptsSite[[s, m]]], {m, 2}], {s, 2}, {col, 2}]]\n    /(QD[ptsSite[[1, 1]]] QD[ptsSite[[2, 1]]])];\nfreeRun[label_, rr_, k_] := Module[{cs, V, Vn, f},\n   cs = Table[With[{ch = chainM[zz]}, LinearSolve[ch[\"P\"], Table[detFree[stt[\"q\"], zz, k, rr], {stt, ch[\"states\"]}]]], {zz, {zX, zP}}];\n   V = cs[[1]] . chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"]; Vn = V/V[[First @ Ordering[-Abs[V], 1]]]; f = fitCell[Vn];\n   {label, N[rr, 10], k, numRank[cs, 10^-40], stabDim[Vn], Lookup[f, \"cell\", \"-\"], Chop[Re[N[Lookup[f, \"abc\", {}], 10]]], sci[Abs[f[\"res\"]]]}];\nfreeTab = {freeRun[\"target c = 1\", rOf[1, 0], 0], freeRun[\"target c = -3/7\", rOf[-3/7, 0], 0],\n   freeRun[\"target c = 2\", rOf[2, 0], 0], freeRun[\"target c = 1, k = 1/2\", rOf[1, 1/2], 1/2],\n   freeRun[\"equal weights (contrast)\", {1, 1}, 0]};\nColumn[{\n  Grid[{{\"t = θ2 - θ1\", tPar}, {\"site x11 points\", ptsSite},\n     {\"cross-ratio of the four points\", ((ptsSite[[2, 1]] - ptsSite[[1, 1]]) (ptsSite[[2, 2]] - ptsSite[[1, 2]]))/((ptsSite[[2, 2]] - ptsSite[[1, 1]]) (ptsSite[[2, 1]] - ptsSite[[1, 2]]))},\n     {\"value required by the E32 pattern\", Simplify[(rotPattern[cc][[1, 1]] rotPattern[cc][[2, 2]])/(rotPattern[cc][[1, 2]] rotPattern[cc][[2, 1]])]},\n     {\"pattern constants vs pole ratios\", {Simplify[rotPattern[cc][[1, 2]]/(cc rotPattern[cc][[1, 1]])], Simplify[(tPar - 2 hX)/(tPar - hX)]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[freeTab, {\"case\", \"{b1/a1, b2/a2}\", \"k\", \"rank{c(z),c(z')}\", \"stabiliser dim\", \"cell\", \"(a,b,c) achieved\", \"rotation residual\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"24223\" data-output-id=\"16\" data-out-n=\"217\" data-sub-idx=\"9\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"39\" data-sub-start=\"17\" data-sub-end=\"22\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[217]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:14.5206em;vertical-align:-7.0103em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.5103em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.5103em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.9078em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.9078em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.8678em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.8678em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:7.2355em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.3678em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.8678em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.4778em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.4551em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">t = </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">2 - </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\