   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result: yes — free weights give the global $E_{32}$ rotation, with real data\n\nWith $t=\\theta_2-\\theta_1$ and the weight ratios\n$$\\frac{b_1}{a_1}=c\\,e^{-kh}\\frac{t}{t-2h},\\qquad \\frac{b_2}{a_2}=c\\,e^{-kh}\\frac{t-2h}{t},$$\nthe determinant equals $\\langle 0|e^{cE_{32}}|\\Psi_A\\rangle/\\langle 0|\\Psi_A\\rangle$ up to normalisation. Checked at 80 digits:\n\n| case | $\\{b_1/a_1,\\,b_2/a_2\\}$ | stabiliser | $(a,b,c)$ | residual |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| target $c=1$ | $\\{0.19149,\\ 5.22222\\}$ | **6** | $(0,0,1)$ | $9\\times10^{-94}$ |\n| target $c=-3/7$ | $\\{-0.08207,\\ -2.23810\\}$ | **6** | $(0,0,-3/7)$ | $5\\times10^{-95}$ |\n| target $c=2$ | — | **6** | $(0,0,2)$ | $3\\times10^{-93}$ |\n| target $c=1$, $k=1/2$ | — | **6** | $(0,0,1)$ | $3\\times10^{-94}$ |\n| equal weights $a_s=b_s$ | $\\{1,1\\}$ | 5 | — | $0.67$ |\n\nAll are twist-independent (rank 1 at $z$ vs $z'$) and land in the big cell. Only $ce^{-kh}$ enters, so $k$ is redundant — with $k=0$ the whole construction is **real and rational in $\\theta$**, unlike the section-12 version which needed a complex $g$.\n\n**Why this version works and section 12's did not.** Here the insertion $u$ and $q_1$ are evaluated at the *same* four points (each site's own $x_{11}$ points), so the weight-independent invariant is the cross-ratio of those points,\n$$\\frac{c_{11}c_{22}}{c_{12}c_{21}}=\\frac{t(t-2h)}{(t-h)^2}=\\frac{784}{423},$$\nwhich is exactly what the $E_{32}$ pattern requires — the pattern constants are themselves pole ratios, $\\tfrac{47}{28}=\\frac{t-2h}{t-h}$ and $\\tfrac{9}{28}=\\frac{t}{t-h}$. In section 12 the insertion sat at the measure pole while $q_1$ was shifted by $h$, which changed the four arguments of the insertion and broke the cross-ratio; no choice of $k$ or of the residue weights could repair it, only a tuned second column.\n\nSo the free weights $a_s,b_s$ are exactly the freedom needed: one ratio per site, and the two conditions of the pattern fix them, with $c_{22}/c_{11}=c^2$ following automatically.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 14. The brackets as contour integrals: the measure is $1/(\\nu_1\\nu_2)$\n\nThe four evaluation points are exactly the zeros of $\\nu_1\\nu_2$:\n$$\\nu_1(u)=(u-\\theta_1-2h)(u-\\theta_2-h),\\qquad \\nu_2(u)=(u-\\theta_1-h)(u-\\theta_2),$$\nso $\\nu_1\\nu_2$ vanishes at $\\theta_1+h,\\ \\theta_1+2h$ (site 1) and $\\theta_2,\\ \\theta_2+h$ (site 2). Hence\n$$\\boxed{\\ \\langle f\\rangle_s=\\oint_{C_s}\\frac{du}{2\\pi i}\\,\\frac{e^{ku}f(u)}{\\nu_1(u)\\nu_2(u)}\\ }$$\nwith $C_s$ encircling that site's two poles (and only those).\n\nPlain residues give $\\frac{b_1}{a_1}=-\\frac{t}{t-2h}$, $\\frac{b_2}{a_2}=-\\frac{t-2h}{t}$, which is the section-13 condition with $c=-1$; the factor $e^{ku}$ multiplies both ratios by $e^{kh}$. So\n$$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}\\langle q_1\\rangle_1&\\langle u\\,q_1\\rangle_1\\\\ \\langle q_1\\rangle_2&\\langle u\\,q_1\\rangle_2\\end{pmatrix}\\Big/\\big(q_1(\\theta_1+h)q_1(\\theta_2)\\big)\\;\\propto\\;\\frac{\\langle 0|e^{cE_{32}}|\\Psi_A\\rangle}{\\langle 0|\\Psi_A\\rangle},\\qquad c=-e^{kh}.$$\nReal $k$ gives all $c<0$; $c=+1$ needs the phase $k=i\\pi/h$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 18. The same object written as contour integrals with measure 1/(nu1 nu2). ---- *)\nClearAll[nu12Poles, nu12Res, brCont, detCont, contRun, contTab];\nnu12Poles = {{(θ1 /. prmX) + hX, (θ1 /. prmX) + 2 hX}, {(θ2 /. prmX), (θ2 /. prmX) + hX}};\n(* residue of 1/(nu1 nu2) at each of the four simple poles *)\nnu12Res[p_] := 1/Times @@ (p - DeleteCases[Flatten[nu12Poles], p]);\nbrCont[f_, s_, k_] := Sum[nu12Res[p] Exp[N[k p, wpS]] f[p], {p, nu12Poles[[s]]}];\ndetCont[qs_, zz_, k_] := Module[{QD = Function[x, Exp[N[x, wpS] Log[N[zz[[1]], wpS]]] (qs[[1]] /. u -> x)]},\n   Det[Table[brCont[Function[p, p^(col - 1) QD[p]], s, k], {s, 2}, {col, 2}]]/(QD[nu12Poles[[1, 1]]] QD[nu12Poles[[2, 1]]])];\ncontRun[k_] := Module[{cs, V, Vn, f},\n   cs = Table[With[{ch = chainM[zz]}, LinearSolve[ch[\"P\"], Table[detCont[stt[\"q\"], zz, k], {stt, ch[\"states\"]}]]], {zz, {zX, zP}}];\n   V = cs[[1]] . chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"]; Vn = V/V[[First @ Ordering[-Abs[V], 1]]]; f = fitCell[Vn];\n   {k, numRank[cs, 10^-40], stabDim[Vn], Chop[N[Lookup[f, \"abc\", {}], 10], 10^-30], N[-Exp[k hX], 10], sci[Abs[f[\"res\"]]]}];\ncontTab = contRun /@ {0, 1/2, -1, I Pi/hX};\nColumn[{\n  Grid[{{\"ν1 zeros\", {(θ1 /. prmX) + 2 hX, (θ2 /. prmX) + hX}}, {\"ν2 zeros\", {(θ1 /. prmX) + hX, (θ2 /. prmX)}},\n     {\"site-1 contour poles\", nu12Poles[[1]]}, {\"site-2 contour poles\", nu12Poles[[2]]},\n     {\"residue ratios {b1/a1, b2/a2} at k = 0\", {nu12Res[nu12Poles[[1, 2]]]/nu12Res[nu12Poles[[1, 1]]], nu12Res[nu12Poles[[2, 2]]]/nu12Res[nu12Poles[[2, 1]]]}},\n     {\"section-13 prediction with c = -1\", rOf[-1, 0]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[contTab, {\"k\", \"rank{c(z),c(z')}\", \"stabiliser dim\", \"(a,b,c) achieved\", \"predicted c = -e^{kh}\", \"rotation residual\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"24223\" data-output-id=\"17\" data-out-n=\"225\" data-sub-idx=\"9\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"42\" data-sub-start=\"13\" data-sub-end=\"18\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[225]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:13.3551em;vertical-align:-6.4276em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.9276em;\"><span style=\"top:-8.9276em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.92em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.92em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.88em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.88em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:7.26em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.38em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.88em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.03em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.06366em;\">ν</span><span class=\"mord\">1 zeros</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.82em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.06366em;\">ν</span><span class=\"mord\">2 zeros</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">site-1 contour poles</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.4em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">site-2 contour poles</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.19em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">residue ratios {b1/a1, b2/a2} at k = 0</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:0.02em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">section-13 prediction with c = -1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.38em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:7.26em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-3.38em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.88em;\"><span style=\"top:-6.03em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size1\">{</span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span