  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result: confirmed — it is that minor\n\nRows $\\alpha=1,2$ over the **full** ladder contour, integrand dressed by $(u-\\theta_1)$, columns $\\{1,u\\}$ of the first column type:\n\n| $k$ | stabiliser | $(a,b,c)$ | $-e^{kh}$ | residual |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| $0$ | **6** | $(0,0,-1)$ | $-1$ | $9\\times10^{-95}$ |\n| $1/2$ | **6** | $(0,0,-1.64872)$ | $-1.64872$ | $3\\times10^{-94}$ |\n| $i\\pi/h$ | **6** | $(0,0,1)$ | $1$ | $3\\times10^{-78}$ |\n\nand the two determinants differ by exactly the predicted constant:\n$$\\frac{\\det(\\text{minor, }\\alpha\\text{ rows})}{\\det(\\text{section 14, site rows})}=1.13572-1.63794\\,i=e^{2\\pi i\\theta_2/h}-e^{2\\pi i\\theta_1/h},$$\nstate-independent to $10^{-73}$ over all 24 states.\n\n**So the picture is uniform.** Everything so far is a minor of one scalar-product-type matrix; what changes is the measure and which rows/columns are kept:\n\n| object | measure | rows × columns | result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| scalar product (§6) | ladder, 5 poles | $6\\times6$, triple $\\times\\ \\alpha$ | $\\langle\\Omega^L_w|$, the surface $b=a(c-a)$ |\n| all 225 minors (§9) | ladder, 5 poles | any $6\\times6$ with content $Q_1^4Q_2^2$ | same $\\langle\\Omega^L_w|$ |\n| this one (§13–15) | $(u-\\theta_1)\\times$ ladder $=1/(\\nu_1\\nu_2)$ | $2\\times2$, $(\\alpha=1,2)\\times(\\beta=0,1)$, $i=1$, $j=3$ | $\\langle0|e^{cE_{32}}$, $c=-e^{kh}$ |\n\nThe polynomial insertion $(u-\\theta_1)$ removing one pole is what drops the object from degree 6 to degree 2 in $q$ and changes which SoV coordinates move ($x_{11}$ only, instead of the full label).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 16. Products of one-site brackets: how much of $e^{c_1E_{32}}\\otimes e^{c_2E_{32}}$ is reachable?\n\nOpen item 2 of the README: the product of two one-site brackets, each a $1\\times1$ determinant with its\nown weights, was conjectured to give the per-site rotation $e^{c_1E_{32}}\\otimes e^{c_2E_{32}}$ with\n**independent** parameters. Also untested: the one-site bracket on the *fundamental* site (only the\nadjoint site was checked in §8).\n\nEach one-site bracket is a two-term functional on that site's two $x_{11}$ points,\n$B_s = Q_1(p_{s,1}) + r_s\\,Q_1(p_{s,2})$, normalised by $Q_1(p_{s,1})$; the ratio $r_s$ is free\n(any measure with poles only at that site's two $x_{11}$ points, dressed by $e^{k_su}$, realises it).\nThe product $B_1B_2$ therefore has a **rank-one** coefficient matrix $c_{ij}=r_1^{i-1}r_2^{j-1}$ on the\nfour $x_{11}$ labels, whereas the per-site rotation pattern is\n$\\begin{pmatrix}1 & \\frac{t-2h}{t-h}c_2\\\\ c_1-\\frac{19}{28}c_2 & c_1c_2\\end{pmatrix}$.\nSo the question is exactly: *when is the per-site rotation pattern rank one?*",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 20. Product of two one-site brackets: the per-site rotation pattern, its rank-one locus, and the realisation. ---- *)\nClearAll[XNinv, e8low, e3low, prodRotV, psC, psSupport, psPat, outerPat, rankRel, locusSol, prodBr, prodRun, prodTab, rr1, rr2, cc1, cc2, natR, kOf, rOfk];\nXNinv = Inverse[XN];\ne8low = UnitVector[d1, d1]; e3low = UnitVector[d2, d2];\n(* exact per-site rotation covector (e8 e^{c1 E32}) x (e3 e^{c2 E32}) and its exact SoV coefficients *)\nprodRotV[c1_, c2_] := Flatten[Outer[Times, e8low . nilExpT2[JJ[3, 2, λ1], c1, d1], e3low . nilExpT2[JJ[3, 2, λ2], c2, d2]]];\npsC = Expand[prodRotV[cc1, cc2] . XNinv];\npsSupport = Flatten @ Position[psC, _?(# =!= 0 &), {1}, Heads -> False];\npsPat = Table[psC[[fourLabels[[i, j]]]], {i, 2}, {j, 2}];\n(* a product of two one-site brackets has a RANK-ONE coefficient matrix on the four x11 labels *)\nouterPat[a_, b_] := {{1, b}, {a, a b}};\nrankRel = Factor[Det[psPat]];\nlocusSol = Solve[Thread[Flatten[psPat] == Flatten[outerPat[rr1, rr2]]], {rr1, rr2, cc2}];\n\n(* realisation: B_s = Q1(p_{s,1}) + r_s Q1(p_{s,2}), normalised; the object is B_1 B_2.\n   A two-pole measure 1/((u-p_{s,1})(u-p_{s,2})) dressed by e^{k_s u} gives r_s = -e^{k_s h}. *)\nrOfk[k_] := -Exp[k hX];\nprodBr[qs_, zz_, rr_] := Module[{QD = Function[x, Exp[N[x, wpS] Log[N[zz[[1]], wpS]]] (qs[[1]] /. u -> x)]},\n   Product[(QD[ptsSite[[s, 1]]] + rr[[s]] QD[ptsSite[[s, 2]]])/QD[ptsSite[[s, 1]]], {s, 2}]];\nprodRun[label_, rr_] := Module[{cs, V, Vn, mat, sv, f1, f2, fc, prod},\n   cs = Table[With[{ch = chainM[zz]}, LinearSolve[ch[\"P\"], Table[prodBr[st[\"q\"], zz, rr], {st, ch[\"states\"]}]]], {zz, {zX, zP}}];\n   V = cs[[1]] . chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"]; Vn = V/V[[First @ Ordering[-Abs[V], 1]]];\n   mat = Partition[Vn, d2]; sv = SingularValueList[mat, Tolerance -> 0];\n   f1 = fitRep[mat[[All, d2]], λ1]; f2 = fitRep[mat[[d1]], λ2]; fc = fitCell[Vn];\n   prod = sv[[2]]/sv[[1]] < 10^-40;   (* rank one 8x3 <=> the covector really is a product *)\n   {label, N[rr, 6], numRank[cs, 10^-40], stabDim[Vn], sci[sv[[2]]/sv[[1]]],\n    Which[Abs[fc[\"res\"]] < 10^-40, \"global rotation \" <> ToString[N[Lookup[fc, \"abc\", {}], 4]],\n      prod && Max[Abs[f1[[2]]], Abs[f2[[2]]]] < 10^-40, \"per-site rotation (c1, c2) = \" <> ToString[{N[f1[[1, 3]], 6], N[f2[[1, 3]], 6]}],\n      prod, \"product, not a rotation\", True, \"not a product, not a rotation\"],\n    sci[Abs[fc[\"res\"]]]}];\n(* natural residue ratios of 1/(nu1 nu2) per site, for reference *)\nnatR = Table[nu12Res[nu12Poles[[s, 2]]]/nu12Res[nu12Poles[[s, 1]]], {s, 2}];\nkOf = Log[47/28]/hX;   (* k2 - k1 that puts the two e^{k_s u}-dressed brackets on the locus *)\n\nprodTab = {\n   prodRun[\"site 1 only (r2 = 0)\", {1/2, 0}],\n   prodRun[\"site 2 only (r1 = 0), fundamental\", {0, 1/2}],\n   prodRun[\"on the locus r2 = (47/28) r1\", {1/2, (1/2) 47/28}],\n   prodRun[\"on the locus, second point\", {-3/5, (-3/5) 47/28}],\n   prodRun[\"off the locus\", {1/2, 1/2}],\n   prodRun[\"natural residue ratios of 1/(nu1 nu2)\", natR],\n   prodRun[\"e^{k u} dressings, k1 = 0, k2 = log(47/28)\", {rOfk[0], rOfk[kOf]}],\n   prodRun[\"e^{k u} dressings, k1 = 1/2, k2 = 1/2 + log(47/28)\", {rOfk[1/2], rOfk[1/2 + kOf]}],\n   prodRun[\"e^{k u} dressings, equal k = 0 (contrast)\", {rOfk[0], rOfk[0]}]};\nColumn[{\n  Grid[{{\"support of the per-site rotation covector\", psSupport},\n     {\"is it inside the four x11 labels?\", SubsetQ[Sort @ Flatten[fourLabels], psSupport]},\n     {\"per-site pattern on the four x11 labels\", MatrixForm[psPat]},\n     {\"det of that pattern (rank-one condition = 0)\", rankRel},\n     {\"rank-one locus: {r1, r2, c2} in terms of c1\", locusSol},\n     {\"(t-2h)/(t-h), (t-h)/(t-2h)\", {(tPar - 2 hX)/(tPar - hX), (tPar - hX)/(tPar - 2 hX)}},\n     {\"natural residue ratios {r1, r2} of 1/(nu1 nu2)\", natR},\n     {\"k2 - k1 on the locus, = log[(t-2h)/(t-h)]/h\", {kOf, N[kOf, 12]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[prodTab,\n    {\"case\", \"{r1, r2}\", \"rank{c(z),c(z')}\", \"stab dim\", \"sigma2/sigma1 (8x3)\", \"verdict\", \"global rotation residual\"}],\n   Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"24223\" data-output-id=\"19\" data-out-n=\"251\" data-sub-idx=\"21\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"48\" data-sub-start=\"44\" data-sub-end=\"55\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[251]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:22.9353em;vertical-align:-11.2177em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:11.7177em;\"><span style=\"top:-14.29em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.29em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.7177em;\"><span style=\"top:-7.6777em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:7.6777em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:10.8553em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-5.1777em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.6777em;\"><span style=\"top:-8.2928em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.4551em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">support of the per-site rotation covector</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.0928em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.4551em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">is it inside the four x11 labels?</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.2777em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.4551em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">per-site pattern on the four x11 labels</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.4774em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.4551em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">det of that pattern (rank-one condition = 0)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.2674em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.4551em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">rank-one locus: {r1, r2, c2} in terms of c1</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.0574em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.4551em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">(t-2h)/(t-h), (t-h)/(t-2h)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:0.1526em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.4551em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">natural residue ratios {r1, r2} of 1/(nu1 nu2)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:1.3626em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.4551em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">k2 - k1 on the locus, = log[(t-2h)/(t-h)]/h</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:5.1777em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:10.8553em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-5.1777em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style