  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result 1 (exact, Gröbner): an object built from site-1 $Q$-values can only be a local $E_{32}$\n\nAn object whose integrand only ever sees site-1 $Q$-values has $c_x$ supported on the **8 labels with\nsite 2 at its base value** — the site-2 factor of $\\Psi_A(x)$ cancels against the normalisation. So ask\nwhich rotations are supported there. The coefficients outside the set generate an ideal in\n$\\mathbb{Q}[a,b,c]$; `Solve` chokes on these systems, `GroebnerBasis` is instant:\n\n| rotations supported inside | Gröbner basis | conclusion |\n|---|---|---|\n| site-1-local, the 8 site-2-base labels | $\\langle b,\\;a\\rangle$ | $a=b=0$: **only $E_{32}$** |\n| site-1-local, the 3 labels of a $2\\times2$ Wronskian minor | $\\langle c,b,a\\rangle$ | nothing but the identity |\n| global $\\langle0|g$, the 8 site-2-base labels | $\\langle c^2,\\;b,\\;19a+9c\\rangle$ | $a=b=c=0$: nothing |\n| global $\\langle0|g$, the 3 Wronskian labels | $\\langle c,b,a\\rangle$ | nothing |\n\nTwo consequences.\n\n1. **No local $E_{21}$ or $E_{31}$ from a site-1-only object**, whatever the measure, the minor shape or\n   the number of $Q_2$ rows. The general site-1-local rotation has support on **12** labels, four of\n   which ($8,11,20,23$) have site 2 moved — $\\langle x|$ are not product states, so even a rotation that\n   acts as the identity on site 2 needs site-2-shifted labels. Only $E_{32}$ escapes this.\n2. It also explains §8 retrospectively: the one-site bracket has global stabiliser 5, not 6, because no\n   *global* rotation lives in that block either.\n\nSo the $E_{21}$/$E_{31}$ directions require an object whose surviving poles sit at **both** sites. The\ntarget is explicit: $\\langle0|e^{aE_{21}}$ is exactly linear in $a$ (all higher powers vanish on\n$\\langle0|$), with\n\n$$c_{x_0}=1,\\qquad c_{(0,1,0|0,0,0)}=-\\tfrac{20}{9}a,\\qquad c_{(1,0,0|0,0,0)}=-\\tfrac{9}{28}a,\\qquad\nc_{(0,0,0|1,0,0)}=\\tfrac{893}{252}a,$$\n\nand **no** doubly-moved label. Dividing out the common factor, the object must be a homogeneous\n**degree-4** expression\n\n$$Q_1(\\theta_1{+}h)W_1(\\theta_1,\\theta_1{-}h)Q_1(\\theta_2)\n+a\\Big[{-\\tfrac{9}{28}}Q_1(\\theta_1{+}2h)W_1(\\theta_1,\\theta_1{-}h)Q_1(\\theta_2)\n-\\tfrac{20}{9}Q_1(\\theta_1{+}h)W_1(\\theta_1{+}h,\\theta_1{-}h)Q_1(\\theta_2)\n+\\tfrac{893}{252}Q_1(\\theta_1{+}h)W_1(\\theta_1,\\theta_1{-}h)Q_1(\\theta_2{+}h)\\Big],$$\n\ni.e. three $Q_1$'s and one $Q_2$: a $4\\times4$ minor of shape (three $i=1$ rows, one $i=2$ row), with\nsite 2's Wronskian frozen. Note the absence of cross terms: a *product* of independent brackets is\nruled out (it would carry $a^2$, $a^3$ terms), so the cancellation has to come from the antisymmetry of\na genuine determinant.\n\n### Result 2 (numerical, complete): no minor of the FSoV matrix with $Q_2$ rows is an SoV expansion\n\nAll minors of the $6\\times6$ scalar-product matrix that contain at least one $i=2$ row, sizes 2 to 5,\nagainst the twist-$w$ vacuum dual $Q$'s, tested with the two-twist criterion of §7:\n\n| shape (#$i{=}1$, #$i{=}2$ rows) | minors | not identically zero | best twist mismatch |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| $(1,1)$ | 540 | 532 | $2.4\\times10^{-1}$ |\n| $(2,1)$ | 1800 | 884 | $4.0\\times10^{-1}$ |\n| $(3,1)$ | 1800 | 9 | $7.7\\times10^{-1}$ |\n| $(2,2)$ | 3375 | 73 | $3.8\\times10^{-1}$ |\n| $(3,2)$ | 1800 | 0 | — |\n\nNot one of the 9315 minors comes anywhere near twist-independence — the *best* mismatch is $O(1)$, not\n$O(10^{-3})$, so this is not a tolerance artefact (the filter accepts anything below $10^{-3}$ and\nre-tests it at 80 digits; nothing survived). **Only the full $(4,2)$ minor, i.e. the whole $6\\times6$, is\nan SoV expansion.** That matches the degree count: $\\Psi_A(x)$ has degree 6, four $Q_1$'s and two\n$Q_2$'s, and a sub-determinant expands into wave functions only if the missing factors are common to\nevery label. Cutting a Wronskian in half does not leave a common factor.\n\nNote the two structural zeros in the table, worth keeping: the size-5 shape $(3,2)$ **vanishes\nidentically** for all 1800 minors, and $(3,1)$ survives in only 9 of 1800 cases.\n\n### What this leaves\n\nThe route to $E_{21}$/$E_{31}$ is *not* a minor of the FSoV matrix. The remaining freedom is the one\n§8 and §13 already used for $E_{32}$: **free weights**. In the row/column form\n$M_{rc}=\\sum_p v^{(r)}_p g_c(p)Q_{i_r}(p+\\sigma_c)$ the FSoV rows only supply two weight profiles\n($v_p=w_p$ and $v_p=w_pe^{2\\pi ip/h}$) out of the 5-dimensional space of weights on the ladder poles.\nThe next test is therefore the $4\\times4$ shape $(3,1)$ with the $v^{(r)}$ free (16 parameters after\nscaling), matched against the explicit degree-4 target above.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 18. Free row weights: the exact linear response of the surface\n\n§17 closes the minors of the FSoV matrix. The freedom it leaves is the one §8 and §13 already used to\nget $E_{32}$: the rows need not carry the ladder measure. Write the $6\\times6$ with **free weights**,\n\n$$M_{mc} \\;=\\; \\sum_{p}v^{(m)}_p\\,\\big[\\text{column }c\\text{ at pole }p\\big],\\qquad\nv^{(m)}_p\\in\\mathbb{C}^5 ,$$\n\nthe base point being the FSoV choice $v^{(m)}_p=w_pe^{2\\pi i(\\alpha_m-1)p/h}$, which is known to give the\nrotation $\\langle\\Omega^L_w|$ on the surface $b=a(c-a)$. The question \"does any weight deformation leave\nthe surface?\" is then a *first-order* question, and it can be answered **exactly**: a determinant is\nmultilinear in its rows, so replacing row $m$'s weights by a single-pole row is precisely the\nderivative $\\partial D/\\partial v^{(m)}_p$ — no finite differences.\n\nThe two properties to preserve are both linear conditions on a deformation $\\delta\\in\\mathbb{C}^{30}$:\n\n1. **Still an SoV expansion.** With $c^{(z)}=c_0+\\varepsilon A$, $c^{(z')}=c_0/\\kappa+\\varepsilon B$,\n   proportionality at first order reads $A-\\kappa B\\in\\mathbb{C}c_0$ — 23 conditions.\n2. **Still a rotation.** $\\langle V|=\\langle V_0|+\\varepsilon\\,\\delta V$ stays in the orbit\n   $\\{\\langle0|g\\}$ iff $\\delta V\\in W:=\\operatorname{span}\\{\\langle V_0|\\rho(X):X\\in\\mathfrak{gl}(3)\\}$\n   (4-dimensional: three orbit directions plus $\\langle V_0|$ itself) — 20 conditions.\n\nTwo families of deformations are known to be allowed and harmless: rescaling any row (6 directions,\nthey only rescale the determinant) and the $e^{ku}$ dressing $v_p\\to v_pe^{kp}$ applied to every row\n(1 direction), which acts as $(a,b,c)\\to(ae^k,be^{2k},ce^k)$ and multiplies $b-a(c-a)$ by $e^{2kh}$,\nhence preserves the surface. So the kernel of the 43 conditions contains at least 7 directions, and\nthe real question is whether it contains more, and whether $\\delta\\big[b-a(c-a)\\big]$ can be nonzero\non it.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 23. Free row weights in the 6x6: exact first-order response of the surface b = a(c-a). ---- *)\nClearAll[poleRow, baseWt, PRall, baseRows, DbaseOf, dDof, c0z, c0zp, kappa, twistRes, V0b, baseFit, a0, b0, c0s,\n  dcz, dczp, dVv, pStar, condTwist, Wmat, Nsp, condRot, Mcond, colNrm, Kker, dirTrivial, dirTrivialN, dABC, dS, respTab, dimTab];\n(* one pole's contribution to a row (alpha-independent); same structure as rowN in section 11 *)\npoleRow[qs_, zz_, qd_, w_, {i_, j_}, p_] := Module[{QD, QU},\n   QD = Function[x, Exp[N[x, wpS] Log[N[zz[[i]], wpS]]] (qs[[i]] /. u -> x)];\n   QU = Function[x, Exp[-N[x, wpS] Log[N[w[[j]], wpS]]] (qd[[j]] /. u -> x)];\n   Flatten @ Table[p^β {-QU[p] QD[p], QU[p] QD[p - hX], QU[p + hX] QD[p]}, {β, 0, 1}]];\nbaseWt[α_] := Table[wSP[[r]] Exp[2 Pi I (α - 1) N[polesSP[[r]], wpS]/hX], {r, Length[polesSP]}];\n(* PRall[zz][[A, m, r]] = pole r's contribution to row m of the 6x6 for state A *)\nPRall[zz_] := PRall[zz] = With[{ch = chainM[zz], qd = vacAtTwist[wM][\"qd\"]},\n   Table[Table[Table[poleRow[st[\"q\"], zz, qd, wM, knownSet[[m, {2, 3}]], polesSP[[r]]],\n      {r, Length[polesSP]}], {m, Length[knownSet]}], {st, ch[\"states\"]}]];\nbaseRows[zz_, A_] := Table[baseWt[knownSet[[m, 1]]] . PRall[zz][[A, m]], {m, Length[knownSet]}];\nDbaseOf[zz_] := DbaseOf[zz] = Table[Det[baseRows[zz, A]]/psi0[zz][[A]], {A, dtot}];\n(* EXACT derivative in the weight v^{(m)}_p: replace row m by that single-pole row *)\ndDof[zz_, m_, r_] := Table[Det[ReplacePart[baseRows[zz, A], m -> PRall[zz][[A, m, r]]]]/psi0[zz][[A]], {A, dtot}];\n\n(* base point: must reproduce section 10's rotation *)\nc0z = Pinv[zX] . DbaseOf[zX]; c0zp = Pinv[zP] . DbaseOf[zP];\npStar = First @ Ordering[-Abs[c0z], 1];\nkappa = c0z[[pStar]]/c0zp[[pStar]];\ntwistRes = Max[Abs[c0z - kappa c0zp]]/Max[Abs[c0z]];\nV0b = c0z . chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"];\nbaseFit = rotFit[V0b];\n{a0, b0, c0s} = baseFit[[1]];\n\n(* the 30 exact directions *)\ndcz = Table[Pinv[zX] . dDof[zX, m, r], {m, Length[knownSet]}, {r, Length[polesSP]}];\ndczp = Table[Pinv[zP] . dDof[zP, m, r], {m, Length[knownSet]}, {r, Length[polesSP]}];\ndVv = Table[dcz[[m, r]] . chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"], {m, Length[knownSet]}, {r, Length[polesSP]}];\n(* condition 1: (A - kappa B) parallel to c0z *)\ncondTwist = Table[With[{v = dcz[[m, r]] - kappa dczp[[m, r]]}, v - (v[[pStar]]/c0z[[pStar]]) c0z],\n   {m, Length[knownSet]}, {r, Length[polesSP]}];\n(* condition 2: dV in W = span{V0 rho(X)} *)\nWmat = Flatten[Table[V0b . Normal[Etot[i, j]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}], 1];\nNsp = NullSpace[Wmat];\ncondRot = Table[Nsp . dVv[[m, r]], {m, Length[knownSet]}, {r, Length[polesSP]}];\n(* combined 43 x 30 system, columns normalised so the rank test is scale-free *)\nMcond = Transpose[Flatten[Table[Join[condTwist[[m, r]], condRot[[m, r]]], {m, Length[knownSet]}, {r, Length[polesSP]}], 1]];\ncolNrm = Table[Max[Abs[Mcond[[All, k]]]], {k, Dimensions[Mcond][[2]]}];\nKker = NullSpace[Transpose[Transpose[Mcond]/colNrm], Tolerance -> 10^-30];\n\n(* the 7 deformations known to be allowed: rescale row m; dress every row by e^{ku} (weight p) *)\ndirTrivial = Join[\n   Table[Flatten[Table[If[m == m0, baseWt[knownSet[[m, 1]]][[r]], 0], {m, Length[knownSet]}, {r, Length[polesSP]}]], {m0, Length[knownSet]}],\n   {Flatten[Table[baseWt[knownSet[[m, 1]]][[r]] polesSP[[r]], {m, Length[knownSet]}, {r, Length[polesSP]}]]}];\ndirTrivialN = (# colNrm) & /@ dirTrivial;   (* same directions in the column-normalised coordinates *)\n(* first-order (a,b,c) and surface response of a direction d in C^30 (unnormalised coordinates) *)\ndABC[d_] := Module[{dV = d . Flatten[dVv, 1], dtn},\n   dtn = dV/V0b[[dtot]] - V0b dV[[dtot]]/V0b[[dtot]]^2;\n   {dtn[[idxA]], 2 dtn[[idxB]], 2 dtn[[idxC]]}];\ndS[d_] := With[{p = dABC[d]}, p[[2]] - (c0s - 2 a0) p[[1]] - a0 p[[3]]];\ndimTab = {\n   {\"base: rotation fit residual / (a,b,c) - (-w1w2, w1, -w1(w2+w3))\", {sci[baseFit[[2]]], Chop[N[baseFit[[1]] - abcOfW[wM], 10], 10^-40]}},\n   {\"base: twist-independence residual, scale kappa\", {sci[twistRes], N[kappa, 10]}},\n   {\"base surface value b - a(c-a)\", sci[Abs[b0 - a0 (c0s - a0)]]},\n   {\"dim W (expect 4) / #rotation conditions\", {dtot - Length[Nsp], Length[Nsp]}},\n   {\"conditions x directions\", Dimensions[Mcond]},\n   {\"dim of the allowed deformation space\", Length[Kker]},\n   {\"do the 7 known-harmless directions satisfy all conditions?\",\n    sci[Max[Table[Max[Abs[Mcond . d]], {d, dirTrivial}]]/Max[Abs[Mcond . First[dirTrivial]] + Max[Abs[Mcond]] 10^-300]]},\n   {\"rank of {allowed space, 7 known directions} (7 = nothing new)\",\n    numRank[Join[Kker, dirTrivialN], 10^-25]}};\nrespTab = Table[With[{d = Kker[[k]]/colNrm}, With[{p = dABC[d]},\n     {k, N[p/Max[Abs[p]], 6], sci[Abs[dS[d]]/Max[Abs[p]]]}]], {k, Length[Kker]}];\nColumn[{\n  Grid[dimTab, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[respTab, {\"allowed direction #\", \"first-order (da, db, dc), normalised\", \"|d[b-a(c-a)]| relative\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<details class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer\">2 warnings</summary><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Power::infy: Infinite expression -------- encountered.                                       -59                                  0. 10</div><div style=\"padding:2px 0 2px 4px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,68,68,0.15)\">Infinity::indet: Indeterminate expression 0. 10    ComplexInfinity encountered.</div></details>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Power::infy: Infinite expression -------- encountered.                                       -59                                  0. 10\nInfinity::indet: Indeterminate expression 0. 10    ComplexInfinity encountered.",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "4f1f0673-7097-4f2a-ac06-839d5b0a171c"
