   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result: the surface is rigid against free weights — and free weights reach exactly its tangent\n\nBase point (cold-rebuilt kernel): twist-independence residual $0$ to 69 digits, rotation fit residual\n$0$ to 71 digits, $(a,b,c)=(-\\frac{35}{6},\\frac52,-\\frac{263}{42})=(-w_1w_2,w_1,-w_1(w_2+w_3))$ exactly,\nand $b-a(c-a)=0$ to 70 digits. The 7 known-harmless directions satisfy all 44 conditions to $10^{-68}$,\nwhich validates the construction.\n\n| quantity | value |\n|---|---|\n| conditions $\\times$ directions | $44\\times30$ (23 twist + 20 rotation + 1 trivial) |\n| $\\dim W$ | 4, as expected |\n| **dim of the allowed deformation space** | **14** |\n| rank of {allowed space, 7 known directions} | 14 — the known ones sit inside it, so there are 7 genuinely new allowed directions |\n| $\\max\\big|\\delta[b-a(c-a)]\\big|/|\\delta(a,b,c)|$ over the 14 | $0$ to 57–65 digits |\n| rank of the induced $(\\delta a,\\delta b,\\delta c)$ | **2** |\n| rank of $\\{\\delta V\\}\\cup\\{V_0\\}$ | 3, i.e. a 2-parameter projective family |\n\nSo free row weights are a real extra freedom — 14 allowed directions rather than the 7 obvious ones —\nbut the extra freedom moves the rotation **along** the surface and never off it. The induced motion in\n$(a,b,c)$ has rank exactly 2, which is the dimension of the surface $b=a(c-a)$ itself: the weights reach\nthe same two-parameter family that varying the dual twist $w$ reaches, and nothing more.\n\nThis extends §10's \"nothing deforms off it\" (225 minors, the $e^{ku}$ dressing, the six permuted vacua)\nto the whole 30-parameter weight family, at first order. Together with §17 it closes the obvious routes:\nthe surface is not an artefact of the FSoV measure.\n\n**What is left for $E_{21}$/$E_{31}$.** Only genuinely nonlinear/structural moves remain:\n\n1. **Finite (not infinitesimal) weight deformations.** First-order rigidity does not forbid a\n   large-weight solution, though it makes one unlikely. The $4\\times4$ shape $(3,1)$ of §17 with free\n   weights is the concrete candidate, matched against the explicit degree-4 target — 16 parameters\n   against 46 conditions, so it needs the structure to conspire, not just a search to be lucky.\n2. **Dual states other than a vacuum.** §10 showed non-vacuum dual $Q$'s stop being rotations, but only\n   for the FSoV weights; the two knobs have never been varied together.\n3. **Change the reference covector.** Everything here is tied to $\\langle0|=e_{24}$ being the\n   lowest-weight covector of $B$. The Weyl-conjugate references of §11 gave the same surface, but a\n   different $B$ (a different SoV basis) would move the whole question.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 19. Independent rotations on the two sites\n\n§16 showed that a *product* of two one-site brackets has a rank-one coefficient pattern on the four\n$x_{11}$ labels, which forces $c_1/c_2=(t-2h)/(t-h)$. But rank one was a property of the product, not of\nthe construction: a genuine $2\\times2$ **determinant** with free weights and a free insertion has more\nknobs. With site $s$ carrying weights $v^{(s)}$ on its two $x_{11}$ points $p_{s,1},p_{s,2}$ and the\nsecond column carrying an insertion $g(u)$,\n\n$$D=\\det\\begin{pmatrix}\\langle Q_1\\rangle_1&\\langle gQ_1\\rangle_1\\\\ \\langle Q_1\\rangle_2&\\langle gQ_1\\rangle_2\\end{pmatrix}\n=\\sum_{i,j}v^{(1)}_iv^{(2)}_j\\big(g(p_{2,j})-g(p_{1,i})\\big)Q_1(p_{1,i})Q_1(p_{2,j}),$$\n\nso the coefficient of the label $(i,j)$ is $c_{ij}\\propto v^{(1)}_iv^{(2)}_j\\big(g(p_{2,j})-g(p_{1,i})\\big)$.\nNormalising $c_{11}=1$, and using the affine freedom $g\\to\\alpha g+\\beta$ to set $g(p_{1,1})=0$,\n$g(p_{2,1})=1$, the free parameters are the two weight ratios $R=v^{(1)}_2/v^{(1)}_1$,\n$S=v^{(2)}_2/v^{(2)}_1$ and the two remaining insertion values $\\gamma=g(p_{1,2})$, $\\delta=g(p_{2,2})$:\n\n$$c_{12}=S\\delta,\\qquad c_{21}=R(1-\\gamma),\\qquad c_{22}=RS(\\delta-\\gamma).$$\n\nThat is **four** unknowns against the **three** ratios of the target pattern\n$\\begin{pmatrix}1&\\frac{47}{28}c_2\\\\ c_1-\\frac{19}{28}c_2&c_1c_2\\end{pmatrix}$, so for each $(c_1,c_2)$ a\none-parameter family of solutions is expected — $\\gamma$ stays free. And since the per-site rotation's\nSoV support is *exactly* those four labels (§16), matching the three ratios matches the entire\n24-component covector; nothing else has to be checked by hand.\n\nBelow: solve for $(R,S,\\delta)$ at a chosen $\\gamma$, build $g$ by interpolation through the four\npoints, and verify the object against the target with the usual tests — twist-independence,\n$\\sigma_2/\\sigma_1$ of the $8\\times3$ matrix (rank one $\\Leftrightarrow$ the covector really is a\nproduct), and a per-site rotation fit in each rep.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 24. Independent per-site rotations e^{c1 E32} (x) e^{c2 E32} from a 2x2 determinant with free weights and a free insertion. ---- *)\nClearAll[psTarget, psSolve, gOf, detFree2, psRun, psTab, RR, SS, gam, del];\n(* the exact target pattern on the four x11 labels, from section 16 *)\npsTarget[c1_, c2_] := psPat /. {cc1 -> c1, cc2 -> c2};\n(* solve c12 = S del, c21 = R (1 - gam), c22 = R S (del - gam) for {R, S, del} at a chosen gam *)\npsSolve[c1_, c2_, gam0_] := Module[{T = psTarget[c1, c2], sol},\n   sol = Solve[{SS del == T[[1, 2]], RR (1 - gam0) == T[[2, 1]], RR SS (del - gam0) == T[[2, 2]]}, {RR, SS, del}];\n   If[sol === {}, Missing[\"no solution\"], First[sol]]];\n(* the insertion: any polynomial through the four prescribed values *)\ngOf[sol_, gam0_] := InterpolatingPolynomial[\n   {{ptsSite[[1, 1]], 0}, {ptsSite[[1, 2]], gam0}, {ptsSite[[2, 1]], 1}, {ptsSite[[2, 2]], del /. sol}}, u];\n(* the object: rows = sites, columns = {1, g}, weights {1, R} and {1, S} on each site's x11 points *)\ndetFree2[qs_, zz_, RS_, g_] := Module[{QD = Function[x, Exp[N[x, wpS] Log[N[zz[[1]], wpS]]] (qs[[1]] /. u -> x)], wts},\n   wts = {{1, RS[[1]]}, {1, RS[[2]]}};\n   Det[Table[Sum[wts[[s, m]] (If[col == 1, 1, g /. u -> ptsSite[[s, m]]]) QD[ptsSite[[s, m]]], {m, 2}], {s, 2}, {col, 2}]]\n    /(QD[ptsSite[[1, 1]]] QD[ptsSite[[2, 1]]])];\npsRun[c1_, c2_, gam0_] := Module[{sol, g, RS, cs, V, Vn, mat, sv, f1, f2, fc},\n   sol = psSolve[c1, c2, gam0];\n   If[MissingQ[sol], Return[{{c1, c2}, gam0, \"no solution\", \"-\", \"-\", \"-\", \"-\"}]];\n   RS = {RR, SS} /. sol; g = gOf[sol, gam0];\n   cs = Table[With[{ch = chainM[zz]}, LinearSolve[ch[\"P\"], Table[detFree2[st[\"q\"], zz, RS, g], {st, ch[\"states\"]}]]], {zz, {zX, zP}}];\n   V = cs[[1]] . chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"]; Vn = V/V[[First @ Ordering[-Abs[V], 1]]];\n   mat = Partition[Vn, d2]; sv = SingularValueList[mat, Tolerance -> 0];\n   f1 = fitRep[mat[[All, d2]], λ1]; f2 = fitRep[mat[[d1]], λ2]; fc = fitCell[Vn];\n   {{c1, c2}, gam0, N[RS, 6], numRank[cs, 10^-40], sci[sv[[2]]/sv[[1]]],\n    {N[f1[[1, 3]], 8], N[f2[[1, 3]], 8]}, sci[Max[Abs[f1[[2]]], Abs[f2[[2]]]]], stabDim[Vn], sci[Abs[fc[\"res\"]]]}];\npsTab = {\n   psRun[1, 2, 2],                (* c1/c2 = 1/2, far off the section-16 locus 47/28 *)\n   psRun[2, 1/2, 2],              (* c1/c2 = 4 *)\n   psRun[-3/7, 5/2, -1],          (* opposite signs, another gamma *)\n   psRun[47/28, 1, 2],            (* ON the section-16 locus, as a control *)\n   psRun[1, 0, 2],                (* site 1 only: should reproduce section 8 *)\n   psRun[0, 1, 2]};               (* site 2 only: impossible for a product of brackets (section 16) *)\nGrid[Prepend[psTab,\n  {\"target (c1, c2)\", \"gamma\", \"{R, S} solved\", \"rank{c(z),c(z')}\", \"sigma2/sigma1 (8x3)\",\n   \"(c1, c2) achieved\", \"per-site fit residual\", \"global stab dim\", \"global rotation residual\"}],\n Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"vscode-wolfram-message-output\" style=\"color:#f44;border-left:3px solid #f44;background:rgba(255,68,68,0.08);padding:2px 6px;margin:1px 0;border-radius:0 3px 3px 0;font-family:monospace;font-size:0.85em;white-space:pre-wrap\">Solve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all &quot;solve&quot; variables.</div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
