   "value": "### Result: **yes** — independent $(c_1,c_2)$ are reachable; §16's obstruction was the product, not the construction\n\nSolving $c_{12}=S\\delta$, $c_{21}=R(1-\\gamma)$, $c_{22}=RS(\\delta-\\gamma)$ for $(R,S,\\delta)$ at a chosen\n$\\gamma$ and interpolating $g$ through the four points gives the target **exactly**, for every\n$(c_1,c_2)$ tried:\n\n| target $(c_1,c_2)$ | $\\gamma$ | $\\{R,S\\}$ | rank$\\{c(z),c(z')\\}$ | $\\sigma_2/\\sigma_1$ | achieved $(c_1,c_2)$ | per-site residual |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| $(1,2)$ | 2 | $\\{\\tfrac{5}{14},-\\tfrac{157}{140}\\}$ | 1 | $7\\times10^{-94}$ | $(1,2)$ | $2\\times10^{-94}$ |\n| $(2,\\tfrac12)$ | 2 | — | 1 | $9\\times10^{-95}$ | $(2,0.5)$ | $1\\times10^{-94}$ |\n| $(-\\tfrac37,\\tfrac52)$ | $-1$ | — | 1 | $3\\times10^{-95}$ | $(-0.4285714,2.5)$ | $3\\times10^{-94}$ |\n| $(\\tfrac{47}{28},1)$ (on §16's locus) | 2 | $\\{-1,\\tfrac{47}{28}\\}$ | 1 | $8\\times10^{-94}$ | $(1.6785714,1)$ | — |\n| $(1,0)$ (site 1 only) | 2 | $\\{-1,0\\}$ | 1 | $1\\times10^{-94}$ | $(1,0)$ | — |\n| $(0,1)$ (site 2 only) | 2 | $\\{\\tfrac{19}{28},\\tfrac{47}{56}\\}$ | 1 | $7\\times10^{-94}$ | $(0,1)$ | $1\\times10^{-94}$ |\n\nEvery row is twist-independent (rank 1), a genuine product covector ($\\sigma_2/\\sigma_1\\sim10^{-94}$),\nand fits a per-site rotation in both reps to $10^{-94}$. All six have global stabiliser dimension 5 and\nglobal rotation residual $O(1)$ — correctly so: a per-site rotation with $c_1\\neq c_2$ is **not** of the\nform $\\langle0|g$ at all, so it is neither on nor off the surface $b=a(c-a)$; that surface is a\nstatement about global rotations only.\n\n**So the whole two-parameter family $e^{c_1E_{32}}\\otimes e^{c_2E_{32}}$ consists of Q-determinants.**\nTwo corrections to what §16 seemed to say:\n\n1. The constraint $c_1/c_2=(t-2h)/(t-h)$ is a property of the **product** of two one-site brackets\n   (its coefficient matrix is rank one), not of bracket objects in general. A $2\\times2$ determinant\n   with a nontrivial insertion has rank-two patterns available and the constraint disappears.\n2. In particular $1\\otimes e^{c_2E_{32}}$ — which §16 showed no product can give — *is* a\n   Q-determinant, with $R=\\tfrac{19}{28}$, $S=\\tfrac{47}{56}$ and a cubic insertion\n   $g(u)=\\tfrac{23675}{11421}+\\tfrac{31375}{5076}u-\\tfrac{59147}{5922}u^2+\\tfrac{37183}{11844}u^3$. The\n   asymmetry between the two sites was an artefact of the product construction too.\n\n**Conventions.** As in §13, each site's bracket is its own two-pole contour integral (its own measure),\nand the insertion $g(u)$ sits in the integrand at the same four points as $Q_1$ — so the\n\"same-points\" requirement of §12 is respected. $\\gamma$ remains free: for each target there is a\none-parameter family of realisations, and $\\gamma$ can be chosen to keep the data real and the\ninsertion low-degree.\n\n**Still open for per-site rotations:** the $E_{21}$/$E_{31}$ directions at a single site. Those need\n$x_{21}$, $x_{22}$ to move, hence $Q_2$ rows. §17's no-go rules out objects built from one site's\n$Q$-values and all FSoV minors, but *not* a two-site object with free weights — which is now the\nobvious thing to try, since free weights are exactly what unlocked this section.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 20. Paul's object: (global $E_{32}$ $2\\times2$ determinant at $k$) $\\times$ (one-site bracket at $k'$)\n\nPaul's construction, to be tested as stated: multiply the two objects already in hand — the $2\\times2$\ndeterminant of §14 that gives the **global** $e^{cE_{32}}$ with $c=-e^{kh}$, and the **one-site** bracket\nof §8 at a *different* parameter $k'$ — and normalise the product by\n$Q_1(\\theta_1{+}h)^2Q_1(\\theta_2)$. Claim: the result is $\\langle0|g_1g_2|\\Psi\\rangle$ up to a\nstate-independent constant, to be checked on all 24 states.\n\nSince $E_{32}^{(1)}$ and $E_{32}^{(2)}$ commute, $g_1g_2=e^{(c+c')E_{32}}\\otimes e^{cE_{32}}$, i.e. a\nper-site pair with independent parameters — which is exactly what §19 built the hard way, so if this\nworks it is much simpler.\n\nThe test below is deliberately more informative than a yes/no. On the four $x_{11}$ labels the wave\nfunction ratios are $\\Psi_A(x)/\\Psi_A(x_0)=X_1^{i-1}X_2^{j-1}$ with\n\n$$X_1=\\frac{Q_1(\\theta_1+2h)}{Q_1(\\theta_1+h)},\\qquad X_2=\\frac{Q_1(\\theta_2+h)}{Q_1(\\theta_2)},$$\n\nso any covector supported on those labels is a polynomial of degree $\\le1$ in each of $X_1,X_2$. The\ncell therefore fits the object over the 24 states against the **six** monomials\n$X_1^aX_2^b$, $a\\le2$, $b\\le1$: the four legitimate ones plus $X_1^2$ and $X_1^2X_2$. That says not\njust whether the claim holds but, if it fails, exactly which monomial spoils it.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 25. Paul's object: detCont(k) * oneSite(k'), normalised by Q1(th1+h)^2 Q1(th2); is it <0|g1 g2|Psi>? ---- *)\nClearAll[QDof, X1of, X2of, oneSiteObj, prodObj, monBasis, monFit, oneSiteFit, cOfObj, overlapPS, pTest, pTab];\nQDof[qs_, zz_, x_] := Exp[N[x, wpS] Log[N[zz[[1]], wpS]]] (qs[[1]] /. u -> x);\nX1of[qs_, zz_] := QDof[qs, zz, ptsSite[[1, 2]]]/QDof[qs, zz, ptsSite[[1, 1]]];\nX2of[qs_, zz_] := QDof[qs, zz, ptsSite[[2, 2]]]/QDof[qs, zz, ptsSite[[2, 1]]];\n(* section 8's one-site bracket, verbatim: measure 1/((u-th1)(u-th1-h)), insertion e^{k'u}, q1(u+h), /q1(th1+h) *)\noneSiteObj[qs_, kp_] := With[{q1 = qs[[1]]},\n   Sum[Exp[N[kp p, wpS]] (q1 /. u -> p + hX)/Times @@ (p - DeleteCases[poles1, p]), {p, poles1}]/(q1 /. u -> poles1[[2]])];\n(* the product. detCont carries 1/(Q1(th1+h) Q1(th2)) and oneSiteObj carries 1/q1(th1+h), so the\n   product is Paul's 1/(Q1(th1+h)^2 Q1(th2)) up to a state-independent twist factor *)\nprodObj[qs_, zz_, k_, kp_] := detCont[qs, zz, k] oneSiteObj[qs, kp];\n\n(* (i) what IS the object? fit over the 24 states against X1^a X2^b, a <= 2, b <= 1.\n   A covector on the four x11 labels can only use a <= 1, so a nonzero X1^2 coefficient is fatal. *)\nmonBasis[qs_, zz_] := With[{x1 = X1of[qs, zz], x2 = X2of[qs, zz]},\n   {1, x1, x2, x1 x2, x1^2, x1^2 x2}];\nmonFit[k_, kp_, zz_] := Module[{ch = chainM[zz], M, D, co},\n   M = Table[monBasis[st[\"q\"], zz], {st, ch[\"states\"]}];\n   D = Table[prodObj[st[\"q\"], zz, k, kp], {st, ch[\"states\"]}];\n   co = LeastSquares[M, D];\n   <|\"coef\" -> co/co[[1]], \"res\" -> Max[Abs[M . co - D]]/Max[Abs[D]]|>];\n(* the one-site factor on its own: should be a(1 + c' X1), giving the local parameter c' *)\noneSiteFit[kp_, zz_] := Module[{ch = chainM[zz], M, D, co},\n   M = Table[{1, X1of[st[\"q\"], zz]}, {st, ch[\"states\"]}];\n   D = Table[oneSiteObj[st[\"q\"], kp], {st, ch[\"states\"]}];\n   co = LeastSquares[M, D];\n   <|\"cLoc\" -> co[[2]]/co[[1]], \"res\" -> Max[Abs[M . co - D]]/Max[Abs[D]]|>];\ncOfObj[k_, kp_, zz_] := With[{ch = chainM[zz]},\n   LinearSolve[ch[\"P\"], Table[prodObj[st[\"q\"], zz, k, kp], {st, ch[\"states\"]}]]];\n(* the claim's right-hand side: <0| e^{c1 E32} (x) e^{c2 E32} |Psi_A> / <0|Psi_A>, all 24 states *)\noverlapPS[c1_, c2_, zz_] := With[{ch = chainM[zz], V = prodRotV[c1, c2]},\n   Table[V . (st[\"vec\"]/st[\"vec\"][[dtot]]), {st, ch[\"states\"]}]];\n\npTest[k_, kp_] := Module[{fit, os, cG, cL, cz, czp, V, Vn, mat, sv, f1, f2, D, T, ratio, ch = chainM[zX]},\n   fit = monFit[k, kp, zX];\n   os = oneSiteFit[kp, zX];\n   cG = -Exp[N[k hX, wpS]];          (* global parameter of detCont, section 14 *)\n   cL = os[\"cLoc\"];                   (* local parameter of the one-site bracket *)\n   cz = cOfObj[k, kp, zX]; czp = cOfObj[k, kp, zP];\n   V = cz . chainM[zX][\"xNorm\"]; Vn = V/V[[First @ Ordering[-Abs[V], 1]]];\n   mat = Partition[Vn, d2]; sv = SingularValueList[mat, Tolerance -> 0];\n   f1 = fitRep[mat[[All, d2]], λ1]; f2 = fitRep[mat[[d1]], λ2];\n   (* the direct test of the claim, on all 24 states, with g1 g2 = e^{(c+c')E32} (x) e^{c E32} *)\n   D = Table[prodObj[st[\"q\"], zX, k, kp], {st, ch[\"states\"]}];\n   T = overlapPS[cG + cL, cG, zX];\n   ratio = D/T;\n   <|\"k\" -> k, \"kp\" -> kp, \"monRes\" -> fit[\"res\"], \"coef\" -> fit[\"coef\"], \"osRes\" -> os[\"res\"],\n     \"cG\" -> cG, \"cL\" -> cL, \"rankZ\" -> numRank[{cz, czp}, 10^-40], \"stab\" -> stabDim[Vn],\n     \"svRatio\" -> sv[[2]]/sv[[1]], \"site1\" -> f1, \"site2\" -> f2,\n     \"nLabels\" -> Length[Select[Abs[cz]/Max[Abs[cz]], # > 10^-40 &]],\n     \"ratioSpread\" -> (Max[Abs[ratio]] - Min[Abs[ratio]])/Max[Abs[ratio]],\n     \"claimDev\" -> Max[Abs[D/Mean[ratio] - T]]/Max[Abs[T]]|>];\npTab = {pTest[0, 0], pTest[0, 1/2], pTest[1/2, -1], pTest[1/2, 1/2]};\nColumn[{\n  Grid[Prepend[Table[{d[\"k\"], d[\"kp\"], N[d[\"cG\"], 6], N[d[\"cL\"], 6], sci[d[\"monRes\"]], N[d[\"coef\"], 5]}, {d, pTab}],\n    {\"k\", \"k'\", \"c (global)\", \"c' (local)\", \"6-monomial fit residual\", \"coefficients of {1, X1, X2, X1X2, X1^2, X1^2X2}\"}],\n   Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left],\n  Grid[Prepend[Table[{d[\"k\"], d[\"kp\"], d[\"rankZ\"], d[\"nLabels\"], d[\"stab\"], sci[d[\"svRatio\"]],\n       sci[d[\"ratioSpread\"]], sci[d[\"claimDev\"]]}, {d, pTab}],\n    {\"k\", \"k'\", \"rank{c(z),c(z')} (1 = SoV expansion)\", \"#SoV labels used\", \"stab dim\", \"sigma2/sigma1\",\n     \"spread of D_A / <0|g1g2|Psi_A> over the 24 states\", \"deviation after the best constant\"}],\n   Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"24223\" data-output-id=\"24\" data-out-n=\"336\" data-sub-idx=\"19\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"61\" data-sub-start=\"53\" data-sub-end=\"61\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[336]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"22\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:12.1106em;vertical-align:-5.8053em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.3053em;\"><span style=\"top:-8.3053em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.2977em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.2977em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.2577em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:5.2577em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:6.0153em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.7577em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.2577em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.4177em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">k</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.2177em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.0126em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.8074em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.6023em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.7577em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:6.0153em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-2.7577em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.2577em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.4177em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">k’</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.2177em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.0126em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.8074em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.6023em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8451em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.655em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.394em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.345em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.7577em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:6.0153em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;verti